WEBVTT

1
-00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:01.274
[dramatic music]

2
00:00:12.619 --> 00:00:14.554
-[whooshing]
-[ethereal chiming]

3
00:00:14.689 --> 00:00:16.824
-[soft clattering]
-[thud]

4
00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:18.960
[ethereal whooshing
and explosion]

5
00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:25.332
-[ethereal music]
-[buzzing]

6
00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:31.338
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain spattering]

7
00:00:33.107 --> 00:00:34.207
[snarling in the distance]

8
00:00:37.177 --> 00:00:39.147
[growling in the distance]

9
00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:50.958
[snarling continues]

10
00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:53.127
[ominous music]

11
00:00:55.495 --> 00:00:56.530
[thudding]

12
00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:00.668
[man 1]
Good to go.

13
00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.406
Charlie Oscar, Charlie Oscar,
Snakebite, how copy? Over.

14
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.575
[static]

15
00:01:09.877 --> 00:01:12.947
-Charlie Oscar, Charlie Oscar.
Snakebite, how copy? Over.
-[growling in the distance]

16
00:01:13.081 --> 00:01:15.116
[static]

17
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.385
They gotta be monitoring.
Crack the whip!

18
00:01:21.055 --> 00:01:23.091
[man 2 speaks indistinctly]

19
00:01:23.825 --> 00:01:25.827
[thunder rumbling]

20
00:01:26.293 --> 00:01:27.161
Oh!

21
00:01:28.295 --> 00:01:31.132
Charlie Oscar, Charlie Oscar.
Snakebite, how copy? Over.

22
00:01:31.298 --> 00:01:33.067
-[radio static]
-[Jericho on radio]
<i>Charlie Oscar Six,</i>

23
00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:35.402
<i>-give me the latest.</i>
-Six, it's Snakebite.

24
00:01:35.535 --> 00:01:37.571
Mission's a bust.
Four down hard.

25
00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:40.607
Requesting emergency extract
from Site Delta. Over.

26
00:01:40.742 --> 00:01:43.610
-[snarling]
<i>-Is the mission complete?</i>

27
00:01:43.745 --> 00:01:46.714
[loudly] Six, be advised,
we cannot continue the mission!

28
00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:49.316
We are down to two!
I say again, we are down

29
00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:50.417
-to two back--
-[gunshot]

30
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.654
[man 2 screaming]

31
00:01:54.321 --> 00:01:55.990
-[growling]
-[gunshots]

32
00:01:56.124 --> 00:01:58.525
-[screaming continues]
-[dramatic music]

33
00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:00.327
[shouts] Where are you?

34
00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:01.328
[roaring]

35
00:02:01.461 --> 00:02:03.497
-[shouts]
-[gunshots]

36
00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:08.936
[grunts, pants]

37
00:02:18.445 --> 00:02:20.347
[panting and shakily breathing]

38
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.949
-[growling]
-[gasps]

39
00:02:29.157 --> 00:02:31.591
-[panting]
-[roaring]

40
00:02:33.728 --> 00:02:35.963
-[music increases]
-[roaring]

41
00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:40.467
-[shouts] You motherfuckers!
-[gunshots]

42
00:02:42.737 --> 00:02:44.739
[shouting]

43
00:02:44.872 --> 00:02:45.740
[crunching]

44
00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:48.441
[echoing snarling]

45
00:02:49.609 --> 00:02:52.379
["Fortunate Son
(Fogerty's Factory Version)"
by John Fogerty]

46
00:02:53.915 --> 00:02:55.950
[whirring]

47
00:03:02.857 --> 00:03:05.293
[engines rumbling]

48
00:03:07.094 --> 00:03:08.930
I take you boys
ain't from around here.

49
00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:13.668
Well, we could tell ya,
but, you know?

50
00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:18.940
-[laughs] I hear that.
<i>-♪ ...when the band</i>
<i>Plays Hail to the Chief ♪</i>

51
00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:22.677
<i>-♪ Ooh, they point</i>
<i>The cannon at you, Lord ♪</i>
-[indistinct chatter]

52
00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.080
<i>♪ It ain't me, it ain't me ♪</i>

53
00:03:26.214 --> 00:03:29.317
<i>♪ I ain't</i>
<i>No senator's son, no! ♪</i>

54
00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:33.420
<i>♪ It ain't me, it ain't me ♪</i>

55
00:03:33.486 --> 00:03:35.923
<i>♪ I ain't no fortunate one ♪</i>

56
00:03:36.991 --> 00:03:40.493
<i>♪ Some folks are born</i>
<i>Silver spoon in hand ♪</i>

57
00:03:40.627 --> 00:03:43.664
<i>♪ Lord, don't they help</i>
<i>Themselves, yeah ♪</i>

58
00:03:44.298 --> 00:03:47.702
<i>♪ But when the taxman</i>
<i>Come to the door ♪</i>

59
00:03:47.835 --> 00:03:50.705
<i>♪ Lord, the house looks like</i>
<i>A rummage sale, yeah ♪</i>

60
00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:55.042
<i>♪ It ain't me, it ain't me ♪</i>

61
00:03:55.176 --> 00:03:57.311
<i>♪ I ain't no millionaire's son ♪</i>

62
00:03:57.444 --> 00:03:58.478
<i>♪ No ♪</i>

63
00:03:58.946 --> 00:04:02.283
<i>♪ It ain't me, it ain't me ♪</i>

64
00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:05.452
<i>♪ I ain't no fortunate one, no ♪</i>

65
00:04:06.821 --> 00:04:10.024
-[man 1] Let's go--
-[indistinct chatter]

66
00:04:10.858 --> 00:04:13.194
[man 2] I need three guards
to cover that jeep
right now, let's go.

67
00:04:13.327 --> 00:04:15.129
[indistinct chatter continues]

68
00:04:15.263 --> 00:04:17.732
[flies buzzing]

69
00:04:17.865 --> 00:04:19.267
[man 3]
Fan out! Fan out!

70
00:04:19.466 --> 00:04:22.770
You two. I want you both
up on that ridge ASAP.

71
00:04:22.904 --> 00:04:24.672
-Yes, sir.
-Jesus fucking Christ.

72
00:04:24.805 --> 00:04:26.473
We're looking
for a Major Wallace.

73
00:04:26.606 --> 00:04:28.976
That'd be me.
Listen, you fuckers!

74
00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.478
You gonna tell me
where the rest of your stash is.

75
00:04:31.544 --> 00:04:32.914
-Yeah?
-[man 4 yelling in the distance]
Tell me where it's at!

76
00:04:33.047 --> 00:04:35.816
Bill Wallace.
S-2, First Field Force.

77
00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:38.518
-[helicopter blades whirring]
-You guys must be the field reps

78
00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:42.189
-I was told to expect.
-So, where is it, Major Wallace?

79
00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:43.958
Just when I thought
I'd seen it all.

80
00:04:44.825 --> 00:04:45.860
Follow me.

81
00:04:47.494 --> 00:04:49.797
-[indistinct chatter]
-You guys are what? CORDS?

82
00:04:49.931 --> 00:04:52.233
MACV? SOG?

83
00:04:52.366 --> 00:04:54.168
-CIA?
-Need to know, Major.

84
00:04:54.302 --> 00:04:57.271
Right. And I clearly
don't need to know.

85
00:04:57.405 --> 00:04:58.706
If you told me, you'd have to--

86
00:04:58.839 --> 00:05:00.374
-That's the drill.
-[woman wailing]

87
00:05:00.507 --> 00:05:01.842
-Sergeant Jensen.
-[man 5] Let's go, let's go.

88
00:05:01.976 --> 00:05:02.944
-Let's go to the...
-Would you please get

89
00:05:03.077 --> 00:05:04.011
this kid a lollipop,

90
00:05:04.145 --> 00:05:05.346
or a shot of morphine,

91
00:05:05.512 --> 00:05:08.349
-or something?
-[speaking in Vietnamese]

92
00:05:08.515 --> 00:05:10.851
For Christ's sake, mama's son,
what is your problem?

93
00:05:12.153 --> 00:05:15.256
I told you, I don't understand
a fucking word you say!

94
00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:17.858
-[Jensen] Okay, come with me.
-She said a demon
took her husband.

95
00:05:18.426 --> 00:05:20.593
-A feathered demon.
-That's what I heard.

96
00:05:20.728 --> 00:05:23.431
-You speak gook?
-A little.
Comes with the territory.

97
00:05:23.563 --> 00:05:26.067
Yeah. We can have
that territory.

98
00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.669
-Truck's over here.
-[cross talk]

99
00:05:28.803 --> 00:05:30.838
[ominous music]

100
00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:37.044
[soft whirring]

101
00:05:37.178 --> 00:05:38.946
Same barrels, Russian markings.

102
00:05:39.447 --> 00:05:42.049
Knew it. What are they for?

103
00:05:44.118 --> 00:05:45.653
-Right.
-[whirring]

104
00:05:45.786 --> 00:05:47.021
[sighing] Oh, shit.

105
00:05:47.154 --> 00:05:49.023
[whirring increases]

106
00:05:50.257 --> 00:05:52.625
-I need to know about that.
My men are out--
-We're done here,

107
00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.128
Major, and so are you.

108
00:05:54.261 --> 00:05:55.595
[man 6]
Sir, Six-Alpha is on the phone.

109
00:05:57.798 --> 00:05:59.734
Charlie Oscar,
Rampage, how copy?

110
00:06:00.368 --> 00:06:01.836
I need to talk to the Six.

111
00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:03.471
-[static]
-[man 7 on radio]
<i>Wait one, Rampage.</i>

112
00:06:03.603 --> 00:06:05.706
Rampage, Charlie Oscar Six.
What do you got?

113
00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.575
<i>One truck, ten barrels,</i>
<i>all with standard markings.</i>

114
00:06:08.709 --> 00:06:10.711
<i>Measure 3.46 on the counter.</i>

115
00:06:10.845 --> 00:06:12.880
Hot as hell. Over.
The NBA driver

116
00:06:13.014 --> 00:06:15.282
is showing early symptoms
of radiation poisoning.

117
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:17.451
<i>This is number five</i>
<i>since we've started the track.</i>

118
00:06:17.952 --> 00:06:19.920
Yeah, a-- any further word
on Snakebite?

119
00:06:20.587 --> 00:06:22.490
Negative.
We overflew both last knowns.

120
00:06:22.622 --> 00:06:24.225
Nothing but bush and more bush.

121
00:06:24.358 --> 00:06:25.625
All right, big army
is gonna come in

122
00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.261
and extract all those civilians.

123
00:06:27.395 --> 00:06:30.164
You just stay tight.
Lock it down and stand by.

124
00:06:30.297 --> 00:06:31.732
-[whooshing]
-[explosions]

125
00:06:31.866 --> 00:06:33.801
-[Wallace shouting] Let's go!
-We're close. I think

126
00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:35.369
-we can pick up
Snakebite's track--
-No, no, no,

127
00:06:35.503 --> 00:06:37.338
n-- no, no. Negative.

128
00:06:37.471 --> 00:06:39.606
That is, uh, too much
of a risk out there.

129
00:06:39.673 --> 00:06:42.777
We are ass-deep
in alligator right now, okay?

130
00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:46.447
We're just gonna mark our time
and-- until I figure
this thing out, all right?

131
00:06:46.613 --> 00:06:48.115
Charlie Oscar Six out.

132
00:06:48.749 --> 00:06:49.750
[clatter]

133
00:06:49.884 --> 00:06:51.318
[man 8]
R4 800.

134
00:06:51.452 --> 00:06:53.254
Make sure Bravo gets out
of the perimeter.

135
00:06:53.387 --> 00:06:54.621
What's the latest on Vulture?

136
00:06:54.722 --> 00:06:56.757
[dramatic tone]

137
00:06:58.726 --> 00:07:00.728
[rain spattering]

138
00:07:00.861 --> 00:07:02.897
[ominous music]

139
00:07:03.397 --> 00:07:04.899
[thunder rumbling]

140
00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.436
[men speaking in Vietnamese]

141
00:07:16.077 --> 00:07:17.645
[thunder rumbling]

142
00:07:17.745 --> 00:07:18.946
-[thud]
-[groans]

143
00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.314
-[blade rings]
-[groans]

144
00:07:20.881 --> 00:07:23.117
-[muffled groaning]
-[grunts]

145
00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:42.436
[softly] All right,
let's rock and roll.

146
00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.439
-[indistinct chatter]
-[laughter]

147
00:07:45.573 --> 00:07:47.508
[thunder rumbling]

148
00:07:48.576 --> 00:07:49.477
[Baker]
Go, go!

149
00:07:53.781 --> 00:07:54.882
Get down, get down.

150
00:07:56.183 --> 00:07:57.118
Go, go, go!

151
00:08:03.023 --> 00:08:04.391
[Keyes]
All right. Here we go, Logan.

152
00:08:08.129 --> 00:08:10.164
[men speaking in Vietnamese]

153
00:08:16.337 --> 00:08:19.707
-[gunshots]
-[indistinct shouting]

154
00:08:19.807 --> 00:08:21.308
[thudding]

155
00:08:21.442 --> 00:08:23.477
-Clear! Go!
-[indistinct shouting
in the distance]

156
00:08:23.611 --> 00:08:26.046
[gunshots]

157
00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:33.721
-[loud explosion]
-[yelling]

158
00:08:34.722 --> 00:08:35.556
[groaning]

159
00:08:36.023 --> 00:08:38.225
-[man 1] Clear!
-[gunshots continue]

160
00:08:40.561 --> 00:08:41.428
Rig it!

161
00:08:45.166 --> 00:08:46.867
[loud explosion]

162
00:08:49.336 --> 00:08:51.105
[Leon]
Sarge, Vulture overwatch.

163
00:08:53.307 --> 00:08:54.175
[man 2]
Touching!

164
00:08:55.109 --> 00:08:56.010
Covering!

165
00:08:57.978 --> 00:09:01.048
Vulture overwatch,
you got eyes on this circus.

166
00:09:01.749 --> 00:09:04.985
Roger that. Got a visual.
Clear to engage. Over.

167
00:09:05.119 --> 00:09:06.754
[gunshots in the distance]

168
00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:08.322
-[gunshot]
-[Logan pants]

169
00:09:08.455 --> 00:09:09.323
Twelve o'clock.

170
00:09:10.624 --> 00:09:11.759
[gunshot]

171
00:09:12.593 --> 00:09:13.761
Eleven o'clock, left hut.

172
00:09:13.861 --> 00:09:15.763
[Logan]
Breathe. Relax.

173
00:09:16.463 --> 00:09:18.599
-Aim. Squeeze.
-[gunshot]

174
00:09:18.766 --> 00:09:20.768
-[gunshots]
-[explosions]

175
00:09:21.235 --> 00:09:23.270
[indistinct shouting]

176
00:09:36.217 --> 00:09:37.251
[gunshot]

177
00:09:38.219 --> 00:09:39.119
He's toast, man.

178
00:09:40.287 --> 00:09:42.122
Breathe. Relax.

179
00:09:42.256 --> 00:09:44.792
-[somber music]
-[softly] Aim. Squeeze.

180
00:09:45.192 --> 00:09:48.128
Vulture Six,
clean house here, man.

181
00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.065
We're good to go. All right.

182
00:09:53.567 --> 00:09:55.269
-All right.
-Just give me a second, okay?

183
00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:57.538
-[exhales deeply]
-You're good.

184
00:09:58.839 --> 00:10:00.441
[rain spattering]

185
00:10:00.574 --> 00:10:01.842
Son of a bitch.

186
00:10:02.343 --> 00:10:03.377
-[grunts]
-[Leon] Bingo.

187
00:10:05.279 --> 00:10:06.213
Covering.

188
00:10:09.416 --> 00:10:11.285
-Jesus fucking God.
-[Baker] Oh, no--

189
00:10:11.418 --> 00:10:13.287
-[man 3] Hey.
-[Baker] Leon!

190
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:16.557
Hang in there.
We got you, we got you.

191
00:10:17.391 --> 00:10:18.325
[Leon]
We got you.

192
00:10:19.326 --> 00:10:20.561
Vulture Overwatch,

193
00:10:21.362 --> 00:10:23.530
two friendlies
on the north side perimeter.

194
00:10:23.665 --> 00:10:25.366
Call the birds and then join us.

195
00:10:25.499 --> 00:10:26.900
[Leon]
Watch out!

196
00:10:27.034 --> 00:10:28.737
-[yells]
-[thudding]

197
00:10:28.869 --> 00:10:31.740
-[blade ringing]
-[Baker] Hey, Sergeant,
find anything?

198
00:10:32.741 --> 00:10:34.041
We checked all the other huts.

199
00:10:34.842 --> 00:10:39.046
-No joy. Looks like these two
are all we gonna get.
-We'll take it.

200
00:10:40.214 --> 00:10:41.915
We'll get you outta here,
fellas.

201
00:10:42.049 --> 00:10:43.450
Get you back to your families.

202
00:10:45.619 --> 00:10:46.755
-[speaks indistinctly]
-[sighs] Oh.

203
00:10:46.887 --> 00:10:48.622
-Too late.
-[Baker] Easy, easy--

204
00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.460
-Fuck.
-Shit, man. You're bleeding.

205
00:10:53.594 --> 00:10:55.496
Ah, shit.

206
00:10:56.297 --> 00:10:58.432
-[helicopter blades whirring]
-Fuck, man.

207
00:10:58.565 --> 00:11:00.634
[music increases]

208
00:11:01.435 --> 00:11:03.437
[Baker]
We going home, boys.

209
00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.439
Vodkas and T-bones for everyone.

210
00:11:05.572 --> 00:11:08.042
-Yeah!
-Courtesy of your favorite
Uncle Samantha.

211
00:11:08.175 --> 00:11:10.477
-Oh, yeah!
-And the rocks pretty crew
from Vulture Squad.

212
00:11:10.611 --> 00:11:11.713
-Whoo!
-Look after him!

213
00:11:11.879 --> 00:11:12.946
-[man 4] ...going home.
-Get some beers,

214
00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.181
-boys. We earned it.
-[man 5] Oh--

215
00:11:14.315 --> 00:11:16.350
[cross talk]

216
00:11:16.483 --> 00:11:18.385
-Yeah, you found me.
-New order, Sarge.

217
00:11:18.519 --> 00:11:20.521
Supposed to get you
and your guys
loaded into the Huey

218
00:11:20.655 --> 00:11:22.156
-and out to the sea--
-Wait, wait, wait.
Who the fuck ordered this?

219
00:11:22.289 --> 00:11:25.326
Some colonel named Jericho.
All I know, Sarge.

220
00:11:25.459 --> 00:11:28.896
Well... [sighs and sniffs]
we're not getting any beer.

221
00:11:28.996 --> 00:11:31.899
-["Time Has Come Today"
by The Chambers Brothers]
-[man 6] Ah, shit.

222
00:11:32.399 --> 00:11:33.735
You gotta be fucking kidding me.

223
00:11:34.435 --> 00:11:36.236
[cross talk]

224
00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:37.905
-Who the fuck is Jericho?
-[laughing]

225
00:11:37.971 --> 00:11:40.007
[helicopter blades whirring]

226
00:11:53.921 --> 00:11:55.589
<i>♪ Time has come today ♪</i>

227
00:11:55.724 --> 00:11:57.558
[muted]

228
00:11:57.692 --> 00:12:00.361
<i>♪ Young hearts</i>
<i>Can go their way ♪</i>

229
00:12:02.162 --> 00:12:04.799
<i>♪ Can't put it off another day ♪</i>

230
00:12:05.999 --> 00:12:08.703
<i>♪ I don't care what others say ♪</i>

231
00:12:09.937 --> 00:12:12.306
<i>♪ They say</i>
<i>We don't listen anyway ♪</i>

232
00:12:13.207 --> 00:12:16.745
<i>-♪ Time has come today ♪</i>
-[man speaking
indistinctly on PA]

233
00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:17.846
<i>♪ Hey ♪</i>

234
00:12:23.617 --> 00:12:27.421
<i>♪ Oh! The rules</i>
<i>Have changed today ♪</i>

235
00:12:28.455 --> 00:12:31.358
<i>-♪ Hey ♪</i>
<i>-♪ I have no place to stay ♪</i>

236
00:12:32.359 --> 00:12:35.496
<i>-♪ Hey ♪</i>
<i>-♪ I'm thinking</i>
<i>About the subway ♪</i>

