473
00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:18.605
-[Miller] Fuck yeah.
-[laughing]

474
00:23:18.672 --> 00:23:20.908
-[helicopter blades whirring]
-[dramatic music]

475
00:23:40.761 --> 00:23:42.463
The fuck is that?

476
00:23:42.629 --> 00:23:44.932
-[beeping]
-That's weird.

477
00:23:46.133 --> 00:23:47.068
What's up?

478
00:23:48.135 --> 00:23:50.004
The equipment's all screwy.

479
00:23:50.137 --> 00:23:51.872
We're still
flying right, though.

480
00:23:52.006 --> 00:23:54.341
We're coming up
on datum point zero.

481
00:23:54.475 --> 00:23:56.410
Skids down in one mike!

482
00:23:57.645 --> 00:23:59.747
One mike! One mike!

483
00:24:01.215 --> 00:24:02.116
One mike!

484
00:24:03.317 --> 00:24:04.285
Whoo!

485
00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:12.026
[indistinct chatter]

486
00:24:14.795 --> 00:24:16.664
[pilot]
Good luck, Vultures.

487
00:24:41.288 --> 00:24:42.223
Gear up.

488
00:24:50.998 --> 00:24:53.434
What was that cutting a path
through the trees
back over there?

489
00:24:53.567 --> 00:24:54.869
Looks like a game trail,

490
00:24:55.503 --> 00:24:56.904
but bigger than I've ever seen.

491
00:24:57.371 --> 00:25:00.107
-Elephants?
-Some fucking
big elephants, Sarge.

492
00:25:00.241 --> 00:25:02.710
-The enemy still uses them.
-Fuck, I can't
understand Jericho.

493
00:25:02.776 --> 00:25:04.411
Would've something about that
instead of talking about

494
00:25:04.545 --> 00:25:06.046
a stupid goddamn tiger
the whole time.

495
00:25:06.180 --> 00:25:08.949
Ah, Jericho's shit
is fucked up, man.

496
00:25:09.083 --> 00:25:11.952
-You cannot trust
that motherfucker.
-[Baker] Cut the shit.

497
00:25:12.086 --> 00:25:15.122
Whatever dinky-di Phoenix
number he's running,
don't mean nothin'.

498
00:25:15.256 --> 00:25:17.758
We got our job,
find those Green Berets.

499
00:25:17.892 --> 00:25:20.027
-Fan out!
-[crickets chirping]

500
00:25:20.161 --> 00:25:22.163
[suspenseful music]

501
00:25:26.467 --> 00:25:28.502
[ominous tone]

502
00:25:32.239 --> 00:25:33.107
[Leon]
What is it?

503
00:25:34.141 --> 00:25:34.975
Track.

504
00:25:35.743 --> 00:25:36.744
[Leon]
Is it our guys?

505
00:25:37.144 --> 00:25:38.746
No. Animal.

506
00:25:39.280 --> 00:25:40.314
Something big.

507
00:25:44.185 --> 00:25:45.386
It's a big bird.

508
00:25:46.587 --> 00:25:50.124
Ostrich, emu, maybe a cassowary.

509
00:25:51.258 --> 00:25:52.426
I studied 'em.

510
00:25:53.961 --> 00:25:55.296
There's another one right there.

511
00:25:55.963 --> 00:25:56.830
[clicks]

512
00:25:59.166 --> 00:26:00.834
Let's backtrack 'em, Leon.

513
00:26:00.968 --> 00:26:02.403
They're weird enough,
I could absolutely see

514
00:26:02.536 --> 00:26:04.004
the green beanies tracking 'em.

515
00:26:04.138 --> 00:26:06.607
-What do you got?
-Jack shit.

516
00:26:07.441 --> 00:26:09.376
Just these big ass
Liberace feathers.

517
00:26:11.412 --> 00:26:14.315
Leon, you ever see
something like this?

518
00:26:15.816 --> 00:26:17.618
No. Never.

519
00:26:19.220 --> 00:26:21.656
-What do you got?
-Yeah, I got a backpack.

520
00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:23.692
Xavier?

521
00:26:25.025 --> 00:26:27.228
Piles of shit. Big piles.

522
00:26:27.361 --> 00:26:31.165
-Don't look at me.
-No. Like guano, but,

523
00:26:31.966 --> 00:26:32.866
but huge.

524
00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.436
[music continues]

525
00:26:37.638 --> 00:26:38.572
[Baker]
Sergeant.

526
00:26:40.374 --> 00:26:41.408
Make sense of that.

527
00:26:42.376 --> 00:26:45.379
[Xavier]
There's a mark here that says
"Research Station Four."

528
00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:47.448
Maybe where they were headed.

529
00:26:48.282 --> 00:26:50.284
Was there anything else
around the pack?

530
00:26:50.417 --> 00:26:52.119
[Logan]
Yeah, 5.56 casings.

531
00:26:52.253 --> 00:26:53.254
5.56?

532
00:26:53.387 --> 00:26:55.022
[Logan]
Yeah. And footprints.

533
00:26:55.155 --> 00:26:57.291
Yeah, uh, two different
kinds of tracks.

534
00:26:57.424 --> 00:27:00.527
US Army issue size tens
and some other shit.

535
00:27:00.662 --> 00:27:02.029
Oh, and it look like struggle.

536
00:27:02.162 --> 00:27:04.398
[ominous music]

537
00:27:05.399 --> 00:27:07.268
[distant screeching]

538
00:27:12.139 --> 00:27:14.141
We follow those tracks
for a klick or two.

539
00:27:14.275 --> 00:27:15.710
-You're on point.
-You got it, boss.

540
00:27:15.843 --> 00:27:17.544
-[Miller] Sir.
-[indistinct chatter]

541
00:27:32.192 --> 00:27:34.228
[crickets chirping]

542
00:27:38.700 --> 00:27:39.900
[grumbling in the distance]

543
00:27:48.275 --> 00:27:50.611
[growling in the distance]

544
00:27:51.912 --> 00:27:54.315
-[growling]
-[sighs]

545
00:27:54.948 --> 00:27:58.419
-[growling and screeching]
-[leaves rustling]

546
00:28:01.021 --> 00:28:03.792
-[twigs snapping]
-Oh, shit.

547
00:28:03.924 --> 00:28:06.327
[growling and screeching
increase]

548
00:28:07.027 --> 00:28:09.296
[leaves rustling]

549
00:28:11.932 --> 00:28:12.801
[gasps]

550
00:28:15.336 --> 00:28:17.571
[breathes heavily]

551
00:28:26.347 --> 00:28:27.514
[softly] Rock apes.

552
00:28:28.382 --> 00:28:31.720
-Fucking things are
all over these hills.
-[panting]

553
00:28:31.919 --> 00:28:33.755
[Logan]
That ain't
no fucking rock apes, man.

554
00:28:34.288 --> 00:28:37.124
-[growling]
-Well, fuck.

555
00:28:37.257 --> 00:28:38.959
[Baker]
Time out. Keep moving.

556
00:28:41.228 --> 00:28:43.230
Whatever that is,
it's moving in this direction.

557
00:28:43.931 --> 00:28:46.133
[growling continues]

558
00:28:53.974 --> 00:28:56.009
[breathes shakily]

559
00:29:03.283 --> 00:29:05.319
[soft growling]

560
00:29:08.589 --> 00:29:11.024
-[screeching]
-[Baker screams]

561
00:29:11.158 --> 00:29:12.827
[Leon shouts]
Something's got Baker!

562
00:29:13.327 --> 00:29:15.329
[screaming]

563
00:29:15.797 --> 00:29:17.832
[grunts]

564
00:29:17.965 --> 00:29:20.601
-[gunshots]
-[roaring]

565
00:29:25.072 --> 00:29:25.973
[screeching]

566
00:29:26.073 --> 00:29:28.175
[footsteps receding]

567
00:29:28.308 --> 00:29:29.176
[Baker grunts]

568
00:29:30.377 --> 00:29:32.279
-[Xavier] Baker!
-[Leon] Sarge!

569
00:29:32.413 --> 00:29:34.081
-[grunting]
-I found him, he's down here!

570
00:29:34.548 --> 00:29:36.818
-I found him! Sarge--
-[Xavier] Is he okay?

571
00:29:36.984 --> 00:29:38.218
-What is that shit?
-You okay?

572
00:29:38.352 --> 00:29:40.053
-Yeah.
-[Leon] That thing looked huge.

573
00:29:40.187 --> 00:29:41.823
-[groans]
-[Xavier] Anyone seen
where it went?

574
00:29:41.989 --> 00:29:43.858
-[groans]
-Fucked if I know, man.

575
00:29:43.991 --> 00:29:46.994
-Could be anywhere now.
-Don't let the shadows
play tricks on you.

576
00:29:47.094 --> 00:29:49.997
Whatever it was, let's get
some distance between us.

577
00:29:50.063 --> 00:29:51.999
-It might not be
that simple, Sarge.
-Why not?

578
00:29:52.566 --> 00:29:54.468
It wasn't scared of us.
And if it's hungry,

579
00:29:54.601 --> 00:29:56.103
it wouldn't be scared
to come back either.

580
00:29:56.236 --> 00:29:57.571
We gotta get out
of its territory.

581
00:29:57.705 --> 00:29:59.540
How much territory
are we talking?

582
00:29:59.674 --> 00:30:01.776
If it's a tiger,
60 square miles.

583
00:30:01.910 --> 00:30:03.444
That's this whole
fucking valley, man.

584
00:30:03.577 --> 00:30:05.512
Yeah! So quit your bitching
and get a hump at it.

585
00:30:05.647 --> 00:30:07.448
-You heard what the colonel
said about tigers.
-[Xavier] Yeah.

586
00:30:07.581 --> 00:30:09.884
Great length.
But that ain't no tiger.

587
00:30:10.017 --> 00:30:14.054
-Yeah, no shit.
-It's nothing we can't handle.
Let's move.

588
00:30:14.588 --> 00:30:17.024
I wanna get
to that research station
before dawn.

589
00:30:17.725 --> 00:30:18.827
Let's hump it.

590
00:30:22.629 --> 00:30:24.531
[growling in the distance]

591
00:30:26.366 --> 00:30:29.970
[speaking in Russian]

592
00:30:33.440 --> 00:30:36.778
[Tolstoy in Russian accent]
Borodin's orders are
to track the Americans.

593
00:30:36.911 --> 00:30:39.980
We engage only if they approach
one of our facilities.

594
00:30:40.581 --> 00:30:43.183
Con Nhen, lead the way.

595
00:30:44.017 --> 00:30:45.687
[in Russian accent]
Such friendly people.

596
00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:49.122
Only been here a week,
and I wish I could stay forever.

597
00:30:49.256 --> 00:30:51.826
-[in Vietnamese accent]
Your bones will.
-[growling in the distance]

598
00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:53.994
[suspenseful music]

599
00:30:57.130 --> 00:30:59.566
Con Nhen, you need to relax.

600
00:31:00.234 --> 00:31:02.269
How do you know if Russian
was telling you a joke?

601
00:31:02.402 --> 00:31:03.972
[crickets chirping]

602
00:31:04.104 --> 00:31:06.708
'Cause they will say, is joke.

603
00:31:16.684 --> 00:31:17.852
Still warm.

604
00:31:19.086 --> 00:31:20.621
Can you pick up the trail?

605
00:31:20.755 --> 00:31:21.723
[branch breaks]

606
00:31:21.856 --> 00:31:23.725
[ominous tone]

607
00:31:24.258 --> 00:31:26.961
Still may be close.
Spread out. Do not engage.

608
00:31:27.929 --> 00:31:30.464
Be lower than the grass.
Be quieter than water.

609
00:31:30.965 --> 00:31:33.367
Yeah. The Americans are pussies.

610
00:31:33.902 --> 00:31:37.337
-We should just--
-Be quiet. Spread out
and keep moving.

611
00:31:41.542 --> 00:31:42.710
[softly] Stupid kid.

612
00:31:44.444 --> 00:31:45.546
Stupid country.

613
00:31:47.682 --> 00:31:49.116
Stupid mosquitoes.

614
00:31:50.584 --> 00:31:52.687
-[growls]
-[groans]

615
00:31:54.756 --> 00:31:55.790
-[snapping]
-[groans]

616
00:32:01.161 --> 00:32:05.132
Tolstoy! Aleksandr's gone.
His riffle's filled with blood.

617
00:32:06.199 --> 00:32:07.735
Are any of your people out here?

618
00:32:09.871 --> 00:32:13.942
-What's so funny?
-Follow the blood trail.

619
00:32:14.842 --> 00:32:16.443
-[gun rattles]
-Go.

620
00:32:20.014 --> 00:32:21.883
[coughs and groans]

621
00:32:23.283 --> 00:32:24.919
-What is it?
-[Tolstoy] Don't look.

622
00:32:25.053 --> 00:32:27.588
What is Tolstoy looking at?
I need to see him.

623
00:32:27.722 --> 00:32:28.522
Let me s--

624
00:32:28.656 --> 00:32:30.692
[ominous music]

625
00:32:34.261 --> 00:32:36.496
[retches and vomits]

626
00:32:37.531 --> 00:32:40.167
We need to find
all the Americans
and kill them all.

627
00:32:41.468 --> 00:32:44.672
Con Nhen, Tolstoy. He's dead.

628
00:32:44.806 --> 00:32:45.707
Let's go.

629
00:32:51.445 --> 00:32:53.480
[music increases]

630
00:32:55.016 --> 00:32:57.317
[growling and screeching
in the distance]

631
00:32:57.919 --> 00:32:59.687
[breathing heavily]

632
00:32:59.821 --> 00:33:01.923
[crickets chirping]

633
00:33:04.424 --> 00:33:07.662
Clear that hole, Keyes.
See what you can find in there.

634
00:33:07.795 --> 00:33:08.963
[Keyes]
Yeah, all right.

635
00:33:09.998 --> 00:33:11.933
What the hell do we think
that was back there?

636
00:33:12.667 --> 00:33:15.268
Heard some Aussies in Phuoc Tuy
talking about gook spooks

637
00:33:15.402 --> 00:33:16.938
stalking them
through the boonies.

638
00:33:17.872 --> 00:33:20.273
Yeah. It was a couple gooks
in a turkey suit

639
00:33:20.407 --> 00:33:23.044
-dragging the sarge. [laughs]
-[chuckles]

640
00:33:23.210 --> 00:33:24.112
I could see that.

641
00:33:24.912 --> 00:33:27.649
Could be some...
unknown species.

642
00:33:27.782 --> 00:33:29.216
I'm telling you guys...

643
00:33:29.316 --> 00:33:30.584
-[suspenseful music]
-[screech in the distance]

644
00:33:30.718 --> 00:33:32.854
...there's monsters out here.

645
00:33:32.987 --> 00:33:33.855
[scoffs]

646
00:33:42.030 --> 00:33:44.732
[snarling in the distance]

647
00:33:50.404 --> 00:33:51.839
-Baker.
-[Baker] Yeah.

648
00:33:56.110 --> 00:33:57.611
[Eli]
We could call it in right now.

649
00:34:00.014 --> 00:34:01.581
Say we didn't find shit.

650
00:34:02.850 --> 00:34:04.085
We can all go home.

651
00:34:08.288 --> 00:34:11.159
[softly] Tunnel goes on forever.
Probably to the other side.

652
00:34:12.259 --> 00:34:14.528
For what it's worth,
I think we're going
the right way.

653
00:34:16.630 --> 00:34:17.631
We go through.

654
00:34:20.768 --> 00:34:21.669
You're on point.

655
00:34:22.502 --> 00:34:23.971
-Miller.
-Sarge.

656
00:34:24.105 --> 00:34:25.006
[Baker]
Ass in the tunnel.

657
00:34:25.139 --> 00:34:26.640
[Miller]
Ah, ass in again.

658
00:34:26.774 --> 00:34:28.176
I swear to God.

659
00:34:28.308 --> 00:34:29.276
Fuck him.

660
00:34:30.178 --> 00:34:32.279
[ominous music]

661
00:34:38.552 --> 00:34:40.788
[loud breathing]

662
00:34:49.596 --> 00:34:51.298
-[gasps]
-[dramatic tone]

663
00:34:54.168 --> 00:34:56.204
[flies buzzing]

664
00:34:57.504 --> 00:34:58.740
[whispering] Son of a bitch.

665
00:35:28.069 --> 00:35:30.337
[growling]

666
00:35:46.821 --> 00:35:48.522
[dramatic music]

667
00:35:48.656 --> 00:35:49.857
[screeches]

668
00:35:49.991 --> 00:35:51.591
-Contact rear!
-[gunshots]

669
00:35:51.726 --> 00:35:53.761
[screeching continues]

670
00:35:53.895 --> 00:35:55.730
-[man 1] Fall back! Move!
-[man 2] Fall back!

671
00:35:55.863 --> 00:35:57.231
[all]
Move! Move! Move!

672
00:35:58.032 --> 00:36:00.433
-[man 3] Go! Come on!
Move, move, move!
-[cross talk]

673
00:36:00.567 --> 00:36:02.670
-[gunshots continue]
-[screeching continues]

674
00:36:03.603 --> 00:36:06.207
Move! Company, light 'em up!

675
00:36:06.373 --> 00:36:08.375
[gunshots]

676
00:36:11.846 --> 00:36:13.147
[man 3]
Clear! Clear!

677
00:36:13.281 --> 00:36:14.182
[man 4]
On your left!

678
00:36:15.183 --> 00:36:17.417
-[man 5] Come up.
-[Xavier] Fall back! Move.

679
00:36:17.551 --> 00:36:19.253
[indistinct shouting]

680
00:36:20.221 --> 00:36:22.256
-[screeching]
-[Xavier] Fall back!

681
00:36:24.225 --> 00:36:26.560
[Baker]
Leon! Leon,
we gotta go this way!

682
00:36:27.728 --> 00:36:29.563
[grunts] Leon!

683
00:36:30.765 --> 00:36:33.000
[Leon shouts]
We lost the other guys,
Sarge! What do we do?

684
00:36:33.134 --> 00:36:35.102
Now, let's kill
these fuckers first!

685
00:36:36.403 --> 00:36:38.739
-Come on!
-[Leon] We gotta go this way.

686
00:36:39.240 --> 00:36:41.042
-[growling]
-[Miller] Hey!

687
00:36:41.175 --> 00:36:43.211
[music continues]

688
00:36:43.711 --> 00:36:47.748
-[screeching]
-We walked
into a fucking nightmare!

689
00:36:47.882 --> 00:36:49.884
Jesus fucking Christ!

690
00:36:53.821 --> 00:36:55.589
[Keyes shouts]
I see an exit, now, let's go!

691
00:36:55.723 --> 00:36:58.425
Baker's missing!
Keep falling back!

692
00:36:58.525 --> 00:37:00.527
-Come on, let's go!
-[Keyes] Logan, come on, man!

693
00:37:00.661 --> 00:37:02.797
-[Xavier] Let's go! Right now!
-[indistinct shouting]

694
00:37:02.930 --> 00:37:05.700
-Fuck you!
-[explosion]

695
00:37:06.834 --> 00:37:08.769
[screeching echoes
in the distance]

696
00:37:08.903 --> 00:37:10.938
[suspenseful music]

697
00:37:14.308 --> 00:37:17.245
-I think we're clear.
-We ain't gonna post up here.

698
00:37:18.545 --> 00:37:19.613
They'll be coming.

699
00:37:20.614 --> 00:37:22.650
[crickets chirping]

700
00:37:23.617 --> 00:37:24.584
Fuck.

701
00:37:32.927 --> 00:37:33.794
Now what?

702
00:37:35.329 --> 00:37:37.198
-The hell were those things?
-[screeching]

703
00:37:38.833 --> 00:37:40.467
-Oh, fuck.
-[growling]

704
00:37:40.567 --> 00:37:43.337
Climb. Climb, now.
Questions later.

705
00:37:45.239 --> 00:37:46.506
[grunting]

706
00:37:46.640 --> 00:37:47.540
Move it!

707
00:37:47.675 --> 00:37:50.244
[dramatic music]

708
00:37:50.378 --> 00:37:52.479
-Shit-- no! [grunting]
-[Leon] Sarge!

709
00:37:52.612 --> 00:37:54.248
[growling]

710
00:37:54.382 --> 00:37:56.817
[gunshots]

711
00:37:58.119 --> 00:38:01.856
-[grunting]
-[screeching]

712
00:38:09.496 --> 00:38:11.032
[snarling]

713
00:38:11.999 --> 00:38:14.634
[panting]

714
00:38:15.502 --> 00:38:16.304
Light.

715
00:38:17.238 --> 00:38:18.172
[grunting] Fuck.

716
00:38:20.074 --> 00:38:21.776
Suppose those things
got the other guys?

717
00:38:21.909 --> 00:38:23.377
Not unless they're bulletproof.

718
00:38:23.510 --> 00:38:25.545
[suspenseful music]

719
00:38:25.680 --> 00:38:26.948
Son of a bitch.

720
00:38:28.316 --> 00:38:30.517
That trail, right over there.

721
00:38:31.518 --> 00:38:33.520
Looks like the same one
we saw coming in earlier.

722
00:38:34.355 --> 00:38:36.857
Yeah, it does.
We should see where it leads.

723
00:38:36.991 --> 00:38:39.026
[crickets chirping]

724
00:38:44.165 --> 00:38:45.532
This is really fucked up, man.

725
00:38:47.068 --> 00:38:49.602
Did the colonel tell you
these fucking things
were out here?

726
00:38:50.371 --> 00:38:53.441
When we link up
with the other guys,
we jump on the radio

727
00:38:53.573 --> 00:38:55.443
and ask Jericho point-blank.

728
00:38:55.575 --> 00:38:58.012
I tell you one thing,
this ain't no fucking recon

729
00:38:58.145 --> 00:38:59.612
looking for a bunch
of lost SF dudes.

730
00:38:59.747 --> 00:39:01.182
Leon, if we want answers,
we're gonna have

731
00:39:01.315 --> 00:39:02.750
to go find 'em ourselves.

732
00:39:03.684 --> 00:39:05.720
[growling in the distance]

733
00:39:06.854 --> 00:39:09.056
I can't believe
I fucking volunteer
for this shit.

734
00:39:10.791 --> 00:39:13.094
-[panting]
-[indistinct muttering]

735
00:39:14.128 --> 00:39:15.463
[screeching in the distance]

736
00:39:19.834 --> 00:39:21.634
-Oh, shit.
-[screeching continues]

737
00:39:21.769 --> 00:39:24.472
-[rustling]
-[growling]

738
00:39:24.604 --> 00:39:26.040
Something's in here, man.

739
00:39:27.375 --> 00:39:29.343
[snarling]

740
00:39:31.012 --> 00:39:32.780
[whispering]
We're fucking surrounded.

741
00:39:34.181 --> 00:39:36.050
Remember I told you
about the voices?

742
00:39:36.183 --> 00:39:38.618
These voices, they're real,
they're real, man.

743
00:39:38.753 --> 00:39:40.488
I'm telling you
they're fucking real.

744
00:39:40.620 --> 00:39:43.124
-I told you.
-[Xavier] Hold your fire.

745
00:39:43.257 --> 00:39:44.859
Baker and Leon
could still be out there.

746
00:39:44.992 --> 00:39:47.762
-[screeching]
-[gasping]

747
00:39:54.035 --> 00:39:56.070
[crickets chirping]

748
00:39:58.272 --> 00:40:00.241
[sighs] Pussies.

749
00:40:00.374 --> 00:40:02.542
[growling]

750
00:40:02.676 --> 00:40:04.912
-[dramatic music]
-[thudding]

751
00:40:24.065 --> 00:40:25.166
[Leon]
Holy shit.

752
00:40:25.966 --> 00:40:28.335
[flies buzzing]

753
00:40:28.936 --> 00:40:30.004
Elephants.

754
00:40:31.505 --> 00:40:32.706
They're fucking huge.

755
00:40:37.244 --> 00:40:39.280
[whispering] Sarge. Sarge!

756
00:40:41.248 --> 00:40:42.216
I don't like this.

757
00:40:42.716 --> 00:40:43.951
We shouldn't fucking be here.

758
00:40:44.452 --> 00:40:46.720
This, this doesn't feel right.

759
00:40:46.854 --> 00:40:47.955
I'm telling you,
something's not right.

760
00:40:48.089 --> 00:40:50.124
[suspenseful music]

761
00:40:52.793 --> 00:40:54.627
This is what we do, Leon.

762
00:40:58.399 --> 00:40:59.967
I picked you for a reason, man.

763
00:41:01.869 --> 00:41:03.204
[sniffles]

764
00:41:04.271 --> 00:41:05.773
-Hmm.
-All right.

765
00:41:28.095 --> 00:41:29.997
-Rockslide.
-[shushes]

766
00:41:30.131 --> 00:41:32.366
[loud breathing]

767
00:41:33.834 --> 00:41:34.802
[whispers] It's asleep.

768
00:41:37.338 --> 00:41:39.373
[loud breathing, grumbling]

769
00:41:50.918 --> 00:41:52.953
[ominous music]

770
00:41:55.523 --> 00:41:56.991
[whispers] God bless--

771
00:42:04.031 --> 00:42:06.734
[whispering] Sir, what do we do?

772
00:42:07.801 --> 00:42:09.837
[growling and screeching]

773
00:42:14.975 --> 00:42:17.011
[growling]

774
00:42:21.882 --> 00:42:22.883
-Run!
-Fuck!

775
00:42:23.751 --> 00:42:25.286
[roaring]

776
00:42:26.754 --> 00:42:27.454
Go!

777
00:42:27.588 --> 00:42:29.623
[dramatic music]

778
00:42:31.025 --> 00:42:32.126
[Baker grunts]

779
00:42:33.794 --> 00:42:34.762
Move it, move it!

780
00:42:35.296 --> 00:42:37.131
[gunshots]

781
00:42:37.264 --> 00:42:38.599
Leon, come on!

782
00:42:42.770 --> 00:42:43.771
Up here!

783
00:42:47.775 --> 00:42:48.576
[grunting]

784
00:42:49.310 --> 00:42:50.177
Down.

785
00:42:53.514 --> 00:42:56.917
[Leon panting]
What the fuck was that?

786
00:42:58.252 --> 00:42:59.853
[crashing and thudding]

787
00:43:04.491 --> 00:43:06.026
[growls]

788
00:43:09.997 --> 00:43:13.000
[roars]

789
00:43:15.169 --> 00:43:17.571
-[grunting]
-[splashing]

790
00:43:17.706 --> 00:43:19.807
[indistinct chatter]

791
00:43:21.942 --> 00:43:23.377
-[Keyes] Fuck, man!
-Fuck this.

792
00:43:23.510 --> 00:43:26.313
-Fucking dinosaurs--
-The fucking Flintstones, man.

793
00:43:26.447 --> 00:43:28.549
This is, this is
fucking bullshit.

794
00:43:28.683 --> 00:43:30.818
I didn't sign on
to kill fucking dinosaurs.

795
00:43:30.951 --> 00:43:32.920
We gotta just keep
our shit together.

796
00:43:33.053 --> 00:43:34.321
Best thing is to find
Baker and Leon

797
00:43:34.455 --> 00:43:36.156
and get the fuck out
of Dodge ASAP.

798
00:43:36.290 --> 00:43:39.226
Find Baker and Leon?
That's fucking bullshit, man.

799
00:43:39.360 --> 00:43:41.128
I ain't going back into that
fucking cave of horrors

800
00:43:41.262 --> 00:43:42.563
for no one or nothin'!

801
00:43:42.697 --> 00:43:44.131
We gotta call
for emergency extraction

802
00:43:44.265 --> 00:43:45.332
right fucking now!

803
00:43:45.466 --> 00:43:47.034
Except Leon
was humping the radio.

804
00:43:47.167 --> 00:43:48.535
-[birds chirping]
-[crickets chirping]

805
00:43:48.670 --> 00:43:49.937
-Fuck!
-Well, we ain't nothing

806
00:43:50.070 --> 00:43:51.505
but sitting bait here.

807
00:43:51.639 --> 00:43:53.007
-Let's move!
-Which way?

808
00:43:53.140 --> 00:43:54.908
-[thudding]
-Towards whatever's making

809
00:43:55.042 --> 00:43:56.610
-all that goddamn noise.
-[Xavier] Move!

810
00:43:57.244 --> 00:43:58.245
Towards it?

811
00:43:58.713 --> 00:44:00.614
-[Keyes] Take point.
-[Xavier] Come on, move!

812
00:44:00.749 --> 00:44:02.850
[ominous music]

813
00:44:03.317 --> 00:44:06.353
-Fuck!
-[growling]

814
00:44:07.488 --> 00:44:11.158
[grunting and groaning]

815
00:44:11.925 --> 00:44:13.360
-[Baker] Oh, fuck.
-[groaning]

816
00:44:13.494 --> 00:44:15.396
[panting]

817
00:44:15.896 --> 00:44:17.598
There's a river
around here somewhere.

818
00:44:17.732 --> 00:44:19.300
I saw it on the map.
If we keep heading down,

819
00:44:19.433 --> 00:44:20.901
-we'll hit it.
-Can it swim?

820
00:44:21.035 --> 00:44:23.971
-[snarling]
-[trees crashing]

821
00:44:24.104 --> 00:44:26.106
-Gotta get there first.
-[both grunting]

822
00:44:26.240 --> 00:44:28.275
[dramatic music]

823
00:44:33.414 --> 00:44:34.982
[roaring]

824
00:44:35.115 --> 00:44:36.785
-Find cover.
-[grunts]

825
00:44:50.197 --> 00:44:51.465
-Come on!
-Fuck!

826
00:44:54.703 --> 00:44:56.270
[roaring]

827
00:44:57.037 --> 00:44:57.971
Over here, the tree!

828
00:44:58.939 --> 00:45:00.675
Come on, move! Get down!

829
00:45:02.009 --> 00:45:04.244
[snarling]

830
00:45:05.379 --> 00:45:07.247
[panting]

831
00:45:09.516 --> 00:45:10.785
[roars]

832
00:45:17.224 --> 00:45:19.794
[snarling]

833
00:45:19.927 --> 00:45:21.962
[suspenseful, ominous music]

834
00:45:29.136 --> 00:45:31.238
[Leon speaks softly]
What are you doing?

835
00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.409
-[explosion]
-[Baker] Go! Go, go, go!

836
00:45:35.542 --> 00:45:37.578
[dramatic music]

837
00:45:43.083 --> 00:45:45.319
[roars]

838
00:45:48.956 --> 00:45:50.090
[Baker]
Come on, let's go!

839
00:45:53.227 --> 00:45:54.194
Let's go!

840
00:45:54.328 --> 00:45:55.329
[gasping]

841
00:45:55.462 --> 00:45:57.464
[water splashing]

842
00:46:00.668 --> 00:46:01.568
Fuck.

843
00:46:02.336 --> 00:46:03.738
[crashing]

844
00:46:03.872 --> 00:46:05.439
[roars]

845
00:46:08.275 --> 00:46:09.977
You airborne qualified, Leon?

846
00:46:10.077 --> 00:46:10.978
What?

847
00:46:11.612 --> 00:46:12.680
[yells]

848
00:46:14.615 --> 00:46:15.683
[roaring]

849
00:46:15.817 --> 00:46:18.485
-[splashing]
-[muffled bubbling]

850
00:46:19.420 --> 00:46:21.455
[gasping]

851
00:46:23.323 --> 00:46:24.224
Leon!

852
00:46:31.666 --> 00:46:33.267
Leon. Leon!

853
00:46:34.501 --> 00:46:36.771
Fuck! [grunts]

854
00:46:37.538 --> 00:46:40.574
Leon! [grunts]
Stay with me, brother.

855
00:46:41.442 --> 00:46:43.243
[grunting]

856
00:46:50.752 --> 00:46:52.119
Stay with me, Leon!

857
00:46:53.187 --> 00:46:54.856
Of course you can swim.

858
00:46:55.022 --> 00:46:57.892
-[yells]
-[in Russian accent]
Hey. Hey! Over here!

859
00:46:59.159 --> 00:47:00.027
Hey!

860
00:47:01.696 --> 00:47:03.464
-[both grunting]
-Follow me.

861
00:47:04.465 --> 00:47:06.600
[grunting]

862
00:47:06.734 --> 00:47:09.036
[snarling]

863
00:47:11.038 --> 00:47:14.374
[roars]

864
00:47:15.042 --> 00:47:15.910
-[grunting]
-[loudly sighs]

865
00:47:16.043 --> 00:47:17.745
[panting]

866
00:47:17.879 --> 00:47:20.047
-Leon. Fuck.
-Your friend, is he alive?

867
00:47:20.849 --> 00:47:22.851
-[snarling]
-Come on, Leon.

868
00:47:23.050 --> 00:47:26.153
-[breathing heavily]
-[somber music]

869
00:47:27.187 --> 00:47:29.423
-Wake up, brother! Wake up.
-[coughs]

870
00:47:30.190 --> 00:47:31.793
[Baker]
Get it out. Get it all out.

871
00:47:31.926 --> 00:47:34.495
[coughs]

872
00:47:34.628 --> 00:47:37.264
-Welcome back, brother.
-American?

873
00:47:38.565 --> 00:47:39.767
Yeah, we're American.

874
00:47:40.935 --> 00:47:42.269
Who the fuck is this?

875
00:47:42.402 --> 00:47:44.672
[pants] My name is Sofia Wagner,

876
00:47:44.806 --> 00:47:46.975
the woman who just
saved your lives,
thank you very much.

877
00:47:48.877 --> 00:47:50.845
I have a place
over that way, my lab.

878
00:47:51.311 --> 00:47:52.579
We should go there quickly.

879
00:47:53.480 --> 00:47:56.250
We'll be safe there from the rex
and the flock of deinonychus.

880
00:47:56.383 --> 00:47:57.752
-We should move.
-Rex?

881
00:47:58.519 --> 00:48:00.087
As in, tyrannosaurus rex?

882
00:48:00.187 --> 00:48:02.289
-[roaring]
-[shushes]

883
00:48:03.590 --> 00:48:05.526
[ominous music]

884
00:48:05.660 --> 00:48:07.695
[growling]

885
00:48:08.262 --> 00:48:11.498
[roar]

886
00:48:15.569 --> 00:48:18.171
[whispers]
How are you even here
if you don't know what that was?

887
00:48:20.374 --> 00:48:22.777
That's the mother tyrannosaur
across the river.

888
00:48:23.678 --> 00:48:26.113
They mate for life,
with the mother
raising the chicks

889
00:48:26.179 --> 00:48:28.148
and the father hunting.
Without the father,

890
00:48:28.282 --> 00:48:30.652
the mother will be forced
to take chicks
on the hunt with her.

891
00:48:31.151 --> 00:48:32.754
The father will do
whatever it takes

892
00:48:32.887 --> 00:48:34.488
to get back
to his territory and family.

893
00:48:34.989 --> 00:48:36.590
We should be safe for now.

894
00:48:36.724 --> 00:48:39.560
Listen, lady.
We're a recon team, seven men.

895
00:48:39.694 --> 00:48:42.329
Got separated when we ran
into those fucking things.

896
00:48:43.196 --> 00:48:45.700
We're not going anywhere else
until I find my team.

897
00:48:45.833 --> 00:48:47.401
If your men are
on the other side of the river,

898
00:48:47.534 --> 00:48:49.037
then they're likely
already dead.

899
00:48:49.804 --> 00:48:52.573
You can take it from me,
and I'm never wrong. This way.

900
00:48:54.308 --> 00:48:56.310
Or you can stay and die,
your choice.

901
00:48:56.443 --> 00:48:58.278
-[birds chirping]
-[Sofia grunts]

902
00:48:58.412 --> 00:49:01.148
["Run Through The Jungle
(John's Version)"
by John Fogerty]

903
00:49:01.248 --> 00:49:02.215
Get up.

904
00:49:03.751 --> 00:49:04.986
[grunting]

905
00:49:08.455 --> 00:49:12.159
<i>♪ Whoa, thought</i>
<i>It was a nightmare ♪</i>

906
00:49:12.860 --> 00:49:15.362
-[muted]
<i>-♪ Lord, it's all so true ♪</i>

907
00:49:16.496 --> 00:49:19.734
<i>♪ They told me</i>
<i>Don't go walking slow ♪</i>

908
00:49:19.867 --> 00:49:22.770
<i>♪ The devil's on the loose ♪</i>

909
00:49:22.904 --> 00:49:25.405
<i>-♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>
-[grumbling]

910
00:49:26.306 --> 00:49:29.176
<i>♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>

911
00:49:29.844 --> 00:49:32.613
<i>♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>

912
00:49:33.447 --> 00:49:36.350
<i>♪ Whoa, don't look back to see ♪</i>

913
00:49:37.517 --> 00:49:40.220
<i>♪ Thought I heard a rumblin' ♪</i>

914
00:49:41.188 --> 00:49:43.557
<i>♪ Calling to my name ♪</i>

915
00:49:44.625 --> 00:49:48.029
<i>♪ Two hundred million</i>
<i>Guns are loaded ♪</i>

916
00:49:48.195 --> 00:49:50.898
<i>-♪ Satan cries, take aim ♪</i>
-[hissing]

917
00:49:51.032 --> 00:49:53.735
<i>♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>

918
00:49:54.568 --> 00:49:57.972
<i>-♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>
-[sniffing]

919
00:49:58.106 --> 00:50:00.808
<i>-♪ Better run</i>
<i>Through the jungle ♪</i>
-[snarling]

920
00:50:01.575 --> 00:50:04.544
<i>♪ Whoa, don't look back to see ♪</i>

921
00:50:10.484 --> 00:50:12.920
[grumbling]

922
00:50:22.063 --> 00:50:23.530
[panting]

923
00:50:23.665 --> 00:50:26.299
[grumbling]

924
00:50:31.304 --> 00:50:32.940
[roaring]

925
00:50:33.841 --> 00:50:37.210
<i>♪ Over on the mountain ♪</i>

926
00:50:37.344 --> 00:50:39.947
<i>♪ Thunder magic spoke ♪</i>

927
00:50:41.149 --> 00:50:43.183
<i>♪ Let the people know... ♪</i>

928
00:50:43.316 --> 00:50:44.686
Guess it don't matter, X.

929
00:50:45.552 --> 00:50:46.520
Where we headed?

930
00:50:47.454 --> 00:50:49.924
We go northeast
until we hit the blue line.

931
00:50:50.692 --> 00:50:52.760
-Looks like a klick or less.
-[birds chirping]

932
00:50:52.894 --> 00:50:56.030
Them notes we found
had it marked
as Research Station Four.

933
00:50:56.164 --> 00:50:58.598
-[rumbling]
-And what about, uh,
Sergeant Baker and Leon?

934
00:50:59.100 --> 00:51:00.400
Baker got the same map.

935
00:51:00.935 --> 00:51:02.335
If they're still alive,

936
00:51:02.469 --> 00:51:04.304
they'll head
in the same direction.

937
00:51:04.438 --> 00:51:05.907
Fucking Jericho.

938
00:51:06.040 --> 00:51:08.142
He had to know something
like this was out here, right?

939
00:51:08.275 --> 00:51:10.577
I doubt it, man. Uh, you know,

940
00:51:10.712 --> 00:51:13.280
if they knew there were
dinosaurs out here,
he'd send an Arc Light strike

941
00:51:13.346 --> 00:51:15.917
and turn this whole thing
into a goddamn parking lot.

942
00:51:16.050 --> 00:51:20.121
I mean, he's a--
he's an evil prick,
but he's not stupid.

943
00:51:20.287 --> 00:51:21.689
Except we're north of the Z.

944
00:51:22.422 --> 00:51:25.660
You think Washington
would strike up here
on some intel of dinosaurs?

945
00:51:26.293 --> 00:51:27.962
Think he'd think
that's as crazy as me.

946
00:51:28.096 --> 00:51:30.330
[laughter]

947
00:51:31.666 --> 00:51:32.767
You doin' all right, man?

948
00:51:33.400 --> 00:51:35.469
Yeah, too much goin' on
to hear anything else.

949
00:51:36.369 --> 00:51:37.705
[Keyes]
Well, that's good.

950
00:51:37.839 --> 00:51:39.073
[Xavier]
Quiet down.

951
00:51:40.007 --> 00:51:41.575
There's still NVA out here.

952
00:51:41.709 --> 00:51:44.611
Fuckin' doubt that, man.
There were gooks out here.

953
00:51:45.213 --> 00:51:47.115
It is fuckin' conch snacks now.

954
00:51:48.515 --> 00:51:51.052
[Miller]
Goddammit, look
at all this dino shit.

955
00:51:51.185 --> 00:51:53.755
-[grumbling]
-[Keyes] That's Eli's. [laughs]

956
00:51:56.556 --> 00:51:58.492
[water lapping]

957
00:51:58.625 --> 00:52:00.594
-[light suspenseful music]
-[panting]

958
00:52:00.728 --> 00:52:03.865
-[birds chirping]
-Welcome to my home, gentlemen.

959
00:52:03.998 --> 00:52:08.069
My home away from home
for one year,
seven months, 11 days.

960
00:52:08.568 --> 00:52:09.971
Research Station Four.

961
00:52:12.840 --> 00:52:13.808
Very good.

962
00:52:16.343 --> 00:52:18.512
[growling and grumbling
in the distance]

963
00:52:22.150 --> 00:52:24.351
There were more like us.
American soldiers.

964
00:52:24.484 --> 00:52:26.854
-Green Berets.
-Green Berets?
What is this?

965
00:52:27.755 --> 00:52:30.691
-[Baker] It's
the best men we have.
-Then they're probably dead.

966
00:52:30.825 --> 00:52:33.027
It's all that happens
in this valley, death.

967
00:52:33.527 --> 00:52:34.594
You survived.

968
00:52:35.362 --> 00:52:36.563
Call me the lucky one.

969
00:52:36.697 --> 00:52:37.932
[creaking]

970
00:52:45.706 --> 00:52:48.876
Don't worry, this is
the safest place to be
in the valley.

971
00:52:49.877 --> 00:52:53.181
Steel-reinforced concrete,
very thick walls,

972
00:52:54.548 --> 00:52:57.551
four stories high on one side.

