-Light it up!
-[Miller] Oh, shit!

1342
01:11:01.269 --> 01:11:03.304
-[gunshots]
-[roaring]

1343
01:11:07.341 --> 01:11:09.277
-Cease fire!
-[Xavier] Cease fire!

1344
01:11:10.778 --> 01:11:12.579
[Keyes choking]

1345
01:11:12.713 --> 01:11:14.982
Keyes! Oh, shit!

1346
01:11:15.116 --> 01:11:16.784
-Keyes!
-[Eli] There he is!

1347
01:11:16.918 --> 01:11:19.020
-[indistinct chatter]
-[gasping and groaning]

1348
01:11:19.586 --> 01:11:21.488
-Oh, shit!
-Fucking help me here.

1349
01:11:21.621 --> 01:11:22.957
-Give me, give me--
-Miller, get in here!

1350
01:11:23.090 --> 01:11:25.793
-[Miller] I'm on it, Sarge!
-[cross talk]

1351
01:11:25.927 --> 01:11:27.962
-Eli, stand watch. Keep it on.
-Put pressure bandage--

1352
01:11:28.095 --> 01:11:30.064
Keep pressure on that.
Eli, stand watch.

1353
01:11:30.197 --> 01:11:34.501
-[cross talk]
-[crying and screaming]

1354
01:11:34.634 --> 01:11:37.004
-They tore
his fucking guts out, Sarge.
-[Keyes] Oh, Jesus! Oh, fuckin--

1355
01:11:37.138 --> 01:11:38.906
Looks like he's been--
he's been run through
a fucking meat grinder.

1356
01:11:39.040 --> 01:11:41.842
-Yeah, I know. [spits]
-[Keyes crying and screaming]

1357
01:11:41.976 --> 01:11:44.045
Miller, Miller.
Get that stretcher out.

1358
01:11:44.178 --> 01:11:45.578
-Leon!
-[Leon] Yeah.

1359
01:11:45.713 --> 01:11:48.115
Grab a couple of poles
to carry him back

1360
01:11:48.249 --> 01:11:50.084
to the research station
for evac.

1361
01:11:50.217 --> 01:11:52.753
Leave him. Those big raptors
will come back

1362
01:11:52.887 --> 01:11:55.089
with their full pack of six,
and when that happens,
we'll all die.

1363
01:11:55.222 --> 01:11:57.590
-If we leave him, we might
have chance of survival--
-I don't give two fucks

1364
01:11:57.725 --> 01:12:00.127
-how bad he's cut up.
He goes with us.
-[speaks indistinctly]

1365
01:12:00.261 --> 01:12:03.764
-[somber music]
-Vultures,
sun sets in half hour.

1366
01:12:03.898 --> 01:12:05.532
I do not wanna be
stumbling around in the dark

1367
01:12:05.666 --> 01:12:07.868
with Marlboro Man passed out
on the stretcher.

1368
01:12:08.002 --> 01:12:10.537
-Rig him in there
and let's roll.
-[crying continues]

1369
01:12:10.603 --> 01:12:12.807
-Here. You can have some weight.
-[Miller] Leon!

1370
01:12:12.940 --> 01:12:15.776
-[Keyes] ...God! Oh, my God!
-[Logan] More bandages,
more bandages.

1371
01:12:15.910 --> 01:12:17.945
-[cross talk]
-Stay on that.

1372
01:12:18.079 --> 01:12:20.114
-You're in the best
of hands, Keyes.
-Fuckin' hurts--

1373
01:12:20.247 --> 01:12:23.384
-What you doing this
twice for in one day, man?
-[crying] Oh, my God.

1374
01:12:24.151 --> 01:12:26.553
Best of hands, brother.
Best of hands.

1375
01:12:27.054 --> 01:12:30.091
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain spattering]

1376
01:12:30.825 --> 01:12:32.827
-[Xavier] Hurry up!
-[Baker] Move, move,
move, move, move, Logan!

1377
01:12:32.960 --> 01:12:34.762
-Move, Logan! Move, Logan!
-[Keyes crying]

1378
01:12:34.895 --> 01:12:36.897
-[Baker] Get the door! Come on!
-[Sofia] ...at the door!

1379
01:12:37.031 --> 01:12:38.366
-[Leon] Got it.
-[Xavier] Move.

1380
01:12:38.565 --> 01:12:40.434
[cross talk]

1381
01:12:40.567 --> 01:12:42.803
-[papers rustling]
-On the table! On the table!

1382
01:12:42.937 --> 01:12:44.338
[Xavier]
Lay him down, lay him down!

1383
01:12:44.805 --> 01:12:46.474
[Logan]
Hey, Keyes, Keyes,
look at me. Look at me.

1384
01:12:46.606 --> 01:12:48.809
-[Baker] Get on that--
-[Logan] You're okay.

1385
01:12:48.943 --> 01:12:50.644
-[Eli] Fuck. Fuck, fuck,
fuck, fuck, fuck.
-[Baker] Keep the pressure

1386
01:12:50.778 --> 01:12:52.113
-on it.
-[cross talk]

1387
01:12:52.246 --> 01:12:53.580
[Sofia]
I've got the light!

1388
01:12:53.647 --> 01:12:55.449
-[Logan] Come on, Keyes--
-Miller, Eli.

1389
01:12:55.582 --> 01:12:58.152
Take perimeter.
Do an ammo count,
premise review.

1390
01:12:58.285 --> 01:12:59.586
-[Miller] On it, Sarge.
-[Logan] Look at me, Keyes.

1391
01:12:59.687 --> 01:13:01.088
-[Xavier] You'll be okay, Keyes.
-Leon!

1392
01:13:01.222 --> 01:13:02.323
-[Leon] Yeah.
-Cover for the sergeant.

1393
01:13:02.456 --> 01:13:04.158
-[Leon] I'm on it.
-[groaning]

1394
01:13:04.291 --> 01:13:05.592
-[Leon] Okay, okay--
-[Baker] Sarge...

1395
01:13:05.726 --> 01:13:06.794
-[Logan]
Breathe, breathe, Keyes.
-...is there

1396
01:13:06.927 --> 01:13:08.162
anything else we can do for him?

1397
01:13:08.295 --> 01:13:09.697
He ain't gonna make it
much longer, Sarge.

1398
01:13:09.830 --> 01:13:11.598
-[Keyes groaning and crying]
-He's bleeding bad.

1399
01:13:11.699 --> 01:13:13.667
Maybe change the dressings,
but I-- I-- I don't know--

1400
01:13:13.801 --> 01:13:16.504
Get some morphine into him
and see what we can do
to stop the bleeding.

1401
01:13:16.636 --> 01:13:19.073
-Let's go.
-[cross talk]

1402
01:13:19.206 --> 01:13:21.675
[Keyes screaming and crying]

1403
01:13:24.211 --> 01:13:25.612
[Leon]
You gotta get
that morphine in right now.

1404
01:13:25.713 --> 01:13:27.248
-[Logan] Keyes, Keyes!
-[Leon] I got-- I got th--

1405
01:13:27.381 --> 01:13:29.517
[breathes shakily]

1406
01:13:29.650 --> 01:13:31.252
[Logan]
Keep your eyes on me.
Eyes on me.

1407
01:13:31.385 --> 01:13:33.087
-[music continues]
-[groaning continues]

1408
01:13:33.220 --> 01:13:34.621
[Logan]
Come on-- I'm coming,
Keyes, I'm coming in.

1409
01:13:34.688 --> 01:13:35.890
-I need you to calm down--
-[Leon] Okay, ready?

1410
01:13:36.023 --> 01:13:36.957
-[Logan] Keyes--
-[Leon] Here we go!

1411
01:13:37.091 --> 01:13:39.393
-[panting]
-We got any more?

1412
01:13:39.527 --> 01:13:40.961
-Where's the other one?
-[Baker] Get the morphine
into him!

1413
01:13:41.095 --> 01:13:42.096
-[cross talk]
-Where the fuck
is the other one?

1414
01:13:42.229 --> 01:13:43.330
Where's the second morphine?

1415
01:13:43.464 --> 01:13:45.032
-[Keyes screams]
-Here we go.

1416
01:13:45.166 --> 01:13:47.068
-Son of a bitch.
-...feel that?
You feel that, man?

1417
01:13:47.201 --> 01:13:49.737
-Keyes. Hey, listen to me.
Take a deep breath.
-There you go--

1418
01:13:49.870 --> 01:13:51.539
[Leon]
Can you breathe?
Can you breathe?

1419
01:13:52.206 --> 01:13:54.641
That's good, that's better.
That's good, man.

1420
01:13:54.708 --> 01:13:56.710
-[cries]
-[Leon] I need you
to stay with me, man.

1421
01:13:56.844 --> 01:13:57.878
Hey. Hey, look at me.

1422
01:13:58.012 --> 01:14:00.047
[indistinct chatter
in the distance]

1423
01:14:00.714 --> 01:14:02.183
[clattering]

1424
01:14:03.050 --> 01:14:04.452
[thunder rumbling]

1425
01:14:04.652 --> 01:14:06.454
Just couldn't help yourself,
could you?

1426
01:14:06.654 --> 01:14:08.456
I did nothing to stop this.

1427
01:14:10.324 --> 01:14:11.192
What?

1428
01:14:11.692 --> 01:14:13.027
The dinosaurs.

1429
01:14:14.829 --> 01:14:18.566
We could've stopped it.
It was just accident.

1430
01:14:19.500 --> 01:14:22.136
[Baker]
An accident?
Why didn't you say this before?

1431
01:14:22.269 --> 01:14:24.505
[Sofia]
I wanted to,
but you are-- [sighs]

1432
01:14:25.406 --> 01:14:28.409
-What?
-You are the enemy.

1433
01:14:30.177 --> 01:14:34.982
Lady, I'm not the one
trying to shoot you or eat you.

1434
01:14:35.116 --> 01:14:38.786
I know, I know. I see that now.
You are good men.

1435
01:14:38.919 --> 01:14:41.222
-You are all good men...
-[thunder rumbling]

1436
01:14:41.355 --> 01:14:43.324
...but I needed
more than good men.

1437
01:14:43.991 --> 01:14:45.893
I needed someone who could stop

1438
01:14:46.026 --> 01:14:47.828
what is happening
in this valley.

1439
01:14:48.696 --> 01:14:51.198
[Xavier]
Baker, we need more eyes
on the perimeter.

1440
01:14:52.032 --> 01:14:53.868
-Leon, help the Sarge.
-[Leon] Yes, Sarge.

1441
01:14:54.001 --> 01:14:55.803
[Xavier]
Leon, cover that window.

1442
01:14:55.936 --> 01:14:59.073
Listen. My mission is
to get my men home,
not fight dinosaurs.

1443
01:14:59.206 --> 01:15:02.776
There won't be a home
if Borodin isn't stopped.

1444
01:15:03.377 --> 01:15:04.745
Look out there!

1445
01:15:06.046 --> 01:15:07.047
[exhales deeply]

1446
01:15:08.282 --> 01:15:10.751
Sofia, what exactly
was going on here?

1447
01:15:10.885 --> 01:15:12.620
[Logan softly]
It's all right. We got you.

1448
01:15:12.753 --> 01:15:14.622
-[suspenseful music]
-Put pressure...

1449
01:15:14.755 --> 01:15:18.926
My husband was
nuclear research scientist.

1450
01:15:20.327 --> 01:15:22.163
My field is paleontology.

1451
01:15:22.796 --> 01:15:25.633
We were sent here
by Soviet madman Borodin

1452
01:15:25.799 --> 01:15:29.036
to do what was
strictly research.

1453
01:15:31.305 --> 01:15:33.541
Nobody conducts
scientific research

1454
01:15:33.741 --> 01:15:36.043
in the middle of a jungle
in the middle of a war.

1455
01:15:36.177 --> 01:15:39.747
Even Russia didn't want
his research on home ground.

1456
01:15:40.548 --> 01:15:42.483
When you are ordered
to do something

1457
01:15:42.616 --> 01:15:45.953
by a man like Borodin,
you do it or you die!

1458
01:15:47.755 --> 01:15:48.622
[exhales sharply]

1459
01:15:49.256 --> 01:15:52.927
When we arrived, this collider
had already been tested.

1460
01:15:54.028 --> 01:15:56.397
We were told that
he was working on wormholes

1461
01:15:56.530 --> 01:15:58.999
so that Soviet Union
could crush America,

1462
01:15:59.133 --> 01:16:01.168
send tanks
onto White House lawn.

1463
01:16:02.770 --> 01:16:05.406
But my husband said
that Borodin...

1464
01:16:06.807 --> 01:16:09.076
-...cut corners, you would say.
-[music continues]

1465
01:16:09.877 --> 01:16:14.481
Particles did not collide
and some elements slingshot
beyond speed of light.

1466
01:16:15.583 --> 01:16:16.450
[exhales sharply]

1467
01:16:17.418 --> 01:16:22.423
Wormhole... opened in the past
and dinosaurs walked through.

1468
01:16:22.556 --> 01:16:24.792
-[thunder rumbling]
-[exhales sharply]

1469
01:16:26.594 --> 01:16:29.797
I came with my husband
because of my knowledge.

1470
01:16:30.798 --> 01:16:31.832
[exhales deeply]

1471
01:16:32.499 --> 01:16:33.534
Best team.

1472
01:16:33.668 --> 01:16:35.670
[melancholic music]

1473
01:16:36.303 --> 01:16:37.538
Where's your husband now?

1474
01:16:38.372 --> 01:16:41.575
[crying] I was out
studying the herbivores
that came through.

1475
01:16:43.377 --> 01:16:45.714
Borodin wanted to... see

1476
01:16:45.846 --> 01:16:48.549
if he could make use
of the dinosaurs.

1477
01:16:50.451 --> 01:16:56.357
I heard cracking of machine guns
and came home... [sobs softly]
to find whole team dead.

1478
01:16:57.726 --> 01:17:00.127
Darling husband included.
And so I've sat here,

1479
01:17:00.261 --> 01:17:02.731
doing the only thing I can
to ease the pain.

1480
01:17:03.831 --> 01:17:07.134
We should have stopped him.
He just left his mess of lizards

1481
01:17:07.268 --> 01:17:10.004
and moved on to rebuild
another collider.

1482
01:17:10.137 --> 01:17:11.405
He won't stop.

1483
01:17:12.506 --> 01:17:15.276
Look at where
playing God got us.

1484
01:17:15.409 --> 01:17:17.311
-[thunder rumbling]
-[softly] Hmm?

1485
01:17:19.179 --> 01:17:20.347
I know.

1486
01:17:23.450 --> 01:17:25.552
[Baker]
You know where this
rebuilt collider is?

1487
01:17:27.388 --> 01:17:29.857
[sniffles] They entered
a river in the mountains.

1488
01:17:31.191 --> 01:17:33.360
He thinks I'm dead,
but I know about it.

1489
01:17:34.595 --> 01:17:36.397
You have to help me
make this right

1490
01:17:36.530 --> 01:17:39.633
or more people
will suffer the consequence.

1491
01:17:39.768 --> 01:17:41.869
[music continues]

1492
01:17:47.141 --> 01:17:49.310
-[Baker] How we looking?
-[Xavier] Uh, not good.

1493
01:17:52.279 --> 01:17:57.351
-[shushes, softly] It's okay.
It's okay, man. It's okay.
-[crying and whimpering]

1494
01:17:57.484 --> 01:17:59.019
-It's all right.
-[Keyes] I wanna go home.

1495
01:17:59.153 --> 01:18:00.387
[Logan]
We're gonna get you
back home, man.

1496
01:18:00.521 --> 01:18:01.756
What you gonna tell
your mama about this?

1497
01:18:01.889 --> 01:18:04.625
-[thunder rumbling]
-[screeching]

1498
01:18:05.893 --> 01:18:08.896
[roaring and sniffing]

1499
01:18:08.962 --> 01:18:11.198
[rain spattering]

1500
01:18:13.334 --> 01:18:15.602
-[Miller] You good?
-[sighs] Yeah.

1501
01:18:16.904 --> 01:18:18.906
[sighs] Yeah, these things
just freak me out, man.

1502
01:18:21.041 --> 01:18:22.142
You can handle it.

1503
01:18:23.610 --> 01:18:24.445
[Eli]
Yeah.

1504
01:18:25.647 --> 01:18:27.514
I'd handle it better
if I had me a drink.

1505
01:18:28.215 --> 01:18:29.917
Should've brought along
that lucky flask.

1506
01:18:31.051 --> 01:18:33.287
[Miller]
Baker catches you
with that flask in the field,

1507
01:18:34.521 --> 01:18:35.923
he's gonna jam it up your ass.

1508
01:18:36.623 --> 01:18:38.559
That little flask
saved my ass one time.

1509
01:18:41.161 --> 01:18:43.665
When you and I were
running for CAV,
before we went to the LURPs...

1510
01:18:43.798 --> 01:18:46.133
[light melancholic music]

1511
01:18:46.266 --> 01:18:48.302
...we're clearing out
this little, uh,

1512
01:18:48.435 --> 01:18:50.504
this little
piss ant village... [sniffs]

1513
01:18:51.038 --> 01:18:52.940
...Charlie jumped out
from behind a pile of bamboo

1514
01:18:53.040 --> 01:18:55.409
and just fucking nailed me
with one round from his SKS.

1515
01:18:55.542 --> 01:18:58.579
The round hit the flask
in my pocket, flattened it,

1516
01:18:58.713 --> 01:19:01.415
but all I got was
knocked in my ass.

1517
01:19:05.252 --> 01:19:07.121
If it hadn't been
for that flask in my pocket...

1518
01:19:09.289 --> 01:19:10.958
-That was God.
-[Eli] Mm.

1519
01:19:11.625 --> 01:19:12.960
But I remember well.

1520
01:19:14.863 --> 01:19:16.230
That what happened after that...

1521
01:19:18.532 --> 01:19:20.401
...never gonna forget
those four people.

1522
01:19:21.669 --> 01:19:22.871
Gonna take more
than a whisky flask

1523
01:19:23.003 --> 01:19:24.471
-to save your ass this time.
-Yeah.

1524
01:19:25.072 --> 01:19:27.074
Gonna take more than God
to save yours.

1525
01:19:29.410 --> 01:19:30.244
Where is he?

1526
01:19:31.278 --> 01:19:33.514
He's not there.
You're here. They're here.

1527
01:19:36.216 --> 01:19:37.317
That's what I believe in.

1528
01:19:38.252 --> 01:19:40.287
[Miller]
You know why I carry
these beads every day?

1529
01:19:41.288 --> 01:19:43.725
I'm asking those people
we killed for forgiveness.

1530
01:19:43.858 --> 01:19:45.693
Nah, the fuckings--
Don't listen to me, man.

1531
01:19:45.827 --> 01:19:48.429
-I'm just fucked up.
-[Logan] Hey, you still
with me, Keyes?

1532
01:19:48.562 --> 01:19:49.898
-Keyes, wake up!
-[Xavier] What?

1533
01:19:50.631 --> 01:19:51.733
[Eli]
Keyes is gonna
fucking die for sure

1534
01:19:51.866 --> 01:19:53.100
if we don't get him
outta here, man.

1535
01:19:53.233 --> 01:19:54.869
[Miller]
He's gonna make it. [sniffs]

1536
01:19:55.002 --> 01:19:58.372
-[roaring in the distance]
-Hey, Sarge, we got movement.

1537
01:19:58.505 --> 01:20:00.541
[ominous music]

1538
01:20:02.009 --> 01:20:03.745
Shit. Need more time.

1539
01:20:04.311 --> 01:20:05.914
What's the ETA
on those choppers?

1540
01:20:06.380 --> 01:20:08.182
Last ETA was about an hour.

1541
01:20:08.315 --> 01:20:10.350
Fucking rotor heads
don't like flying at night.

1542
01:20:10.484 --> 01:20:12.019
-[Baker] Fuck.
-Can we hold for an hour?

1543
01:20:12.152 --> 01:20:15.122
They still out there,
just pacing the perimeter.

1544
01:20:15.255 --> 01:20:17.324
Logan, need you out here.

1545
01:20:17.458 --> 01:20:18.726
[Logan]
You're gonna get
to the other side of this,

1546
01:20:18.860 --> 01:20:20.862
-you're gonna be fine.
-Go. I got him.

1547
01:20:20.994 --> 01:20:23.263
-Hang in there. I'll be back.
-[Baker] Grab your left.

1548
01:20:24.231 --> 01:20:26.233
[thunder rumbling]

1549
01:20:26.366 --> 01:20:28.202
[roaring in the distance]

1550
01:20:30.370 --> 01:20:33.540
-What's going on?
-Let me know when you got
a target you can shoot.

1551
01:20:33.675 --> 01:20:36.109
[growling]

1552
01:20:43.383 --> 01:20:44.752
[softly]
He's just walking around.

1553
01:20:45.619 --> 01:20:46.620
[Baker]
You got a shot?

1554
01:20:47.655 --> 01:20:49.223
You want me to give away
our position?

1555
01:20:50.624 --> 01:20:52.059
They already know we're here.

1556
01:20:55.562 --> 01:20:57.732
-Lost it.
-Stay on it.

1557
01:20:59.667 --> 01:21:02.971
-Pretty smart for a bird.
-Way too smart for a bird.

1558
01:21:03.103 --> 01:21:05.339
Listen, man, I found out
some shit talking to the woman.

1559
01:21:05.472 --> 01:21:06.975
-[roaring]
-[shouts] Oh, shit,
they're inside!

1560
01:21:07.107 --> 01:21:09.476
-There's a bird!
-[roaring]

1561
01:21:09.610 --> 01:21:11.980
[gunshots]

1562
01:21:12.112 --> 01:21:14.147
[dramatic music]

1563
01:21:15.148 --> 01:21:16.583
[Xavier]
Get on it. Left, left.

1564
01:21:17.451 --> 01:21:18.418
Shit, it's here!

1565
01:21:19.486 --> 01:21:20.420
[Baker]
Go, go!

1566
01:21:25.192 --> 01:21:28.095
-[indistinct shouting]
-Miller!

1567
01:21:29.196 --> 01:21:31.298
-[man 1] Spread out!
-[man 2] Yeah! Let's go!

1568
01:21:31.431 --> 01:21:32.299
Left!

1569
01:21:37.005 --> 01:21:39.540
-Motherfucker!
-[Miller] Here,
here, here, here!

1570
01:21:41.743 --> 01:21:42.643
[man 3]
Cease fire!

1571
01:21:43.176 --> 01:21:44.111
Cease fire!

1572
01:21:45.312 --> 01:21:46.648
Everyone, full mag.

1573
01:21:47.180 --> 01:21:48.115
[gun cocks]

1574
01:21:49.817 --> 01:21:51.920
It's probing us,
goddamn it, it's probing us.

1575
01:21:52.119 --> 01:21:53.587
[suspenseful music]

1576
01:21:53.721 --> 01:21:56.290
Eyes on, eyes on.
Quick as you can.

1577
01:21:59.326 --> 01:22:00.294
[thud]

1578
01:22:02.697 --> 01:22:05.132
[thudding]

1579
01:22:05.265 --> 01:22:07.134
[growling]

1580
01:22:07.634 --> 01:22:09.269
-[Baker] The fuck is that?
-Got it.

1581
01:22:10.170 --> 01:22:11.739
[gunshots]

1582
01:22:11.873 --> 01:22:13.206
[clinking]

1583
01:22:16.978 --> 01:22:19.881
-[screeching]
-[gunshots]

1584
01:22:20.014 --> 01:22:22.050
[dramatic music]

1585
01:22:22.549 --> 01:22:23.483
[yells] Fuck!

1586
01:22:26.553 --> 01:22:27.621
[Baker]
On your left! Whoa!

1587
01:22:30.157 --> 01:22:32.492
[shouts] Get out!

1588
01:22:33.226 --> 01:22:35.063
-[roaring]
-[yelling]

1589
01:22:35.195 --> 01:22:37.364
-[Baker] Fall back! Fall back!
-[Eli] Fall back!

1590
01:22:40.068 --> 01:22:41.903
[Baker]
Go, go, go, go! Go, go, go, go!

1591
01:22:43.203 --> 01:22:44.371
Leon, move!

1592
01:22:47.507 --> 01:22:49.576
[roaring and growling]

1593
01:22:52.245 --> 01:22:54.048
There are six in the flock
that came through!

1594
01:22:54.181 --> 01:22:56.249
They will find a way!
They always find a way!

1595
01:22:56.383 --> 01:22:58.318
Hey, don't worry about it.
Our chopper's
on its way, okay?

1596
01:22:58.452 --> 01:23:01.188
-[glass shatters]
-[Baker] Shit. Up top!

1597
01:23:01.254 --> 01:23:02.322
-[Xavier] Up, up!
-[Baker] Up top!

1598
01:23:02.456 --> 01:23:04.993
[gunshots]

1599
01:23:05.693 --> 01:23:07.561
-[thudding]
-[glass shatters]

1600
01:23:07.695 --> 01:23:10.798
-Son of a bitch!
-[indistinct shouting]

1601
01:23:11.331 --> 01:23:13.467
He won't survive an hour!
Your men still die!

1602
01:23:13.600 --> 01:23:16.637
-What would you have me do?
-There's a boat
on the docks outside.

1603
01:23:16.771 --> 01:23:18.405
-There's a boat there?
-Yes, it needs fixing,

1604
01:23:18.538 --> 01:23:20.307
that is not my skill.
Your men can.

1605
01:23:20.942 --> 01:23:22.677
Look, there's a escape hole
over there, the vents.

1606
01:23:22.810 --> 01:23:24.277
-Fuck--
-Trust me!

1607
01:23:24.411 --> 01:23:28.783
Open it. Everybody, we're
moving out through the vent!

1608
01:23:28.916 --> 01:23:32.020
-Leon, give Sofia a hand.
-Okay, we're gonna do
a new LZ, Keyes, okay?

1609
01:23:32.219 --> 01:23:34.055
-We're gonna move you to--
-[Keyes] I can't, I can't.

1610
01:23:34.221 --> 01:23:36.858
-Move, Keyes. Grab a leg.
-[Keyes] Put me in the corner.

1611
01:23:36.991 --> 01:23:38.693
-[Baker] Huh?
-[Keyes] Corner!

1612
01:23:38.826 --> 01:23:40.928
-Put me in the fucking corner.
-He wants to go in the corner.

1613
01:23:41.062 --> 01:23:42.063
[Logan]
No, no, no, no,
no, no, no, we--

1614
01:23:42.229 --> 01:23:43.363
-He wants to go.
-We--

1615
01:23:43.497 --> 01:23:44.531
-It's his decision.
-...man.

1616
01:23:44.666 --> 01:23:46.500
-We're not doing--
-Three, two, one.

1617
01:23:46.633 --> 01:23:48.468
[Keyes groans]

1618
01:23:48.602 --> 01:23:49.503
Move it!

1619
01:23:51.538 --> 01:23:52.907
-[Logan] What are we doing?
-[Sofia] We need
to open this vent.

1620
01:23:53.041 --> 01:23:55.076
-[cross talk]
-God be with you, Keyes.

1621
01:23:55.242 --> 01:23:56.410
-God be--
-[Baker] Go, go, go, go.

1622
01:23:56.543 --> 01:23:57.645
[Sofia shouts]
Sergeant!

1623
01:23:58.245 --> 01:24:00.380
-Give me a grenade.
-I gotcha, I gotcha.

1624
01:24:00.514 --> 01:24:03.017
-I got you. I got you.
-Fuck no, man. Don't do this.

1625
01:24:03.151 --> 01:24:04.852
-Give me
a fucking grenade and go.
-[Baker] I got you.

1626
01:24:04.986 --> 01:24:06.553
-[thudding]
-[roaring]

1627
01:24:06.688 --> 01:24:07.889
[Xavier]
Let's go, let's go!

1628
01:24:08.022 --> 01:24:09.623
-[Sofia] Go!
-[Keyes breathing heavily]

1629
01:24:09.757 --> 01:24:12.160
-Man--
-Oh, my God.

1630
01:24:12.894 --> 01:24:15.529
-[Logan] Baker.
-You're not going anywhere
humping a fucking casualty.

1631
01:24:15.663 --> 01:24:17.497
-Be quick!
-[speaks indistinctly]

1632
01:24:17.631 --> 01:24:18.666
I can't do this
without you, man.

1633
01:24:18.800 --> 01:24:20.001
-Yeah, you can--
-I can't.

1634
01:24:20.134 --> 01:24:21.703
-The voices in my head--
-...you fucking can!

1635
01:24:21.836 --> 01:24:23.971
-[crying]
-You fucking listen to me.

1636
01:24:24.105 --> 01:24:25.505
Th-- they're trying to hurt you.

1637
01:24:25.639 --> 01:24:27.175
-[thudding]
-[roaring]

1638
01:24:27.641 --> 01:24:29.677
-You want a cigarette?
-[shakily] Yeah.

1639
01:24:30.144 --> 01:24:32.412
-Okay. Let's go.
-[crying]

1640
01:24:32.546 --> 01:24:34.581
[somber music]

1641
01:24:35.850 --> 01:24:36.718
[gasps]

1642
01:24:37.317 --> 01:24:38.886
Here you go. Enjoy that. Okay.

1643
01:24:39.020 --> 01:24:40.788
-[mumbles]
-[Baker] Logan!

1644
01:24:40.922 --> 01:24:43.623
[glass shatters]

1645
01:24:43.758 --> 01:24:45.292
You're a goddamn hero, man.

1646
01:24:47.061 --> 01:24:50.363
G-- go. F-- fucking go.

1647
01:24:50.497 --> 01:24:53.433
-Fucking go, man!
-[thudding continues]

1648
01:24:55.069 --> 01:24:57.637
[growling]

1649
01:24:58.873 --> 01:25:00.540
[roars]

1650
01:25:03.610 --> 01:25:07.481
Come get some,
you Foghorn Leghorn
motherfuckers.

1651
01:25:07.614 --> 01:25:09.449
-[music increases]
-[clinking]

1652
01:25:10.785 --> 01:25:13.054
[indistinct chatter]

1653
01:25:14.321 --> 01:25:16.356
[explosion]

1654
01:25:17.959 --> 01:25:20.360
[Baker]
All right. Let's get
this old lady started.

1655
01:25:21.996 --> 01:25:23.330
[Sofia]
The back. The back.

1656
01:25:44.986 --> 01:25:47.688
<i>♪ That's one, two</i>
<i>Three, four, five ♪</i>

1657
01:25:48.189 --> 01:25:50.858
<i>♪ I'm psychotic, Keyes's alive ♪</i>

1658
01:25:56.463 --> 01:25:59.399
Doesn't seem right,
leaving Keyes behind
with those lizard birds.

1659
01:26:00.935 --> 01:26:02.737
He's in God's good hands, man.

1660
01:26:03.570 --> 01:26:04.604
What's going on, man?

1661
01:26:05.740 --> 01:26:07.041
We heading north, Sarge?

1662
01:26:07.975 --> 01:26:08.843
Yeah, that's right.

1663
01:26:10.377 --> 01:26:11.545
Would you mind telling me why?

1664
01:26:14.182 --> 01:26:15.917
Vultures, let's bring it in.

1665
01:26:16.050 --> 01:26:18.085
[water lapping gently]

1666
01:26:20.021 --> 01:26:21.022
Listen, um...

1667
01:26:22.389 --> 01:26:24.125
...Keyes was
a tough one to lose,

1668
01:26:24.258 --> 01:26:26.093
particularly knowing now
that we were sent here

1669
01:26:26.227 --> 01:26:27.627
on a bullshit mission.

1670
01:26:28.296 --> 01:26:31.065
But here we are,
in the deepest of shit.

1671
01:26:31.531 --> 01:26:33.600
Last comms with command said
they were sending chopper

1672
01:26:33.734 --> 01:26:36.070
as soon as we sent them
a POS REP for the extract.

1673
01:26:37.437 --> 01:26:42.642
We got maybe one shot at that
with what little juice we have
left in our last radio battery.

1674
01:26:43.911 --> 01:26:44.879
That's one thing.

1675
01:26:45.012 --> 01:26:46.881
[light suspenseful music]

1676
01:26:47.014 --> 01:26:48.850
The other just might be
more important.

1677
01:26:51.152 --> 01:26:54.554
We stumbled
on some real nasty stuff.

1678
01:26:54.689 --> 01:26:57.424
Some Soviet shithead,
name of Borodin,

1679
01:26:58.025 --> 01:27:00.261
has been brewing
out here in the jungle.

1680
01:27:01.229 --> 01:27:03.597
It's a end-of-the-world shit,

1681
01:27:03.731 --> 01:27:04.999
and we just can't leave it.

1682
01:27:05.766 --> 01:27:09.003
Fuck yeah, we can!
We can do that in a heartbeat.

1683
01:27:09.469 --> 01:27:12.439
-End-of-the-world shit's
not our deal.
-The Sarge made the call, Eli,

1684
01:27:12.539 --> 01:27:15.609
-we're already on the way.
-How the hell can
some dipshit Russian dude

1685
01:27:15.743 --> 01:27:17.444
destroy the whole fucking world?

1686
01:27:17.510 --> 01:27:19.714
[Sofia]
You've all seen
what could happen,

1687
01:27:19.847 --> 01:27:21.548
and that was accident!

1688
01:27:22.216 --> 01:27:24.986
Again, that is not
our fucking business, Sarge.

1689
01:27:25.786 --> 01:27:27.621
Th-- this is us
in the chain of command.

1690
01:27:27.755 --> 01:27:30.124
Here's where
end-of-the-world shit
gets sorted out.

1691
01:27:30.725 --> 01:27:32.492
That's presidents
and generals shit.

1692
01:27:33.661 --> 01:27:37.331
-That's Jericho level.
-Do you trust Jericho, Eli?

1693
01:27:39.166 --> 01:27:40.201
Do you trust him?

1694
01:27:41.501 --> 01:27:43.371
Maybe not Jericho, Sarge, but--

1695
01:27:43.503 --> 01:27:44.739
Nobody, Miller.

1696
01:27:45.973 --> 01:27:49.043
No god, no country,

1697
01:27:49.710 --> 01:27:53.281
no man should have
this fucking power!

1698
01:27:53.915 --> 01:27:56.984
This fucking thing
will make hydrogen bombs

1699
01:27:57.617 --> 01:27:59.921
look like Eli lighting
one of his farts.

1700
01:28:00.054 --> 01:28:02.089
[music continues]

1701
01:28:03.724 --> 01:28:06.160
I-- I do have some pretty
powerful farts, Sarge.

1702
01:28:06.294 --> 01:28:08.362
-[growling in the distance]
-Shut the fuck up, man.

1703
01:28:08.495 --> 01:28:09.529
[chuckles]

1704
01:28:11.399 --> 01:28:12.499
This is worse.

1705
01:28:13.633 --> 01:28:17.004
-No man should have that power.
-Hmm. Damn straight.

1706
01:28:19.606 --> 01:28:22.310
Let's keep this
simple as possible,
given the circumstances.

1707
01:28:22.877 --> 01:28:25.512
We find it, tag it,
send in all the bombers we have.

1708
01:28:25.646 --> 01:28:27.514
No. No!

1709
01:28:27.614 --> 01:28:30.151
No, you can't do that.
You can't d--

1710
01:28:30.818 --> 01:28:32.619
-[thudding]
-Oh, fu-- fuck.

1711
01:28:32.753 --> 01:28:34.322
Sarge, take the wheel.

1712
01:28:34.521 --> 01:28:36.556
-[Eli] What's wrong with her?
-She's dope sick.

1713
01:28:37.191 --> 01:28:39.827
Oh, good. We're following
a junkie in to hell.

1714
01:28:39.961 --> 01:28:42.629
[dramatic music]

1715
01:28:42.763 --> 01:28:44.865
[grumbling]

1716
01:28:52.306 --> 01:28:55.109
I said it right from the start,
there are monsters out here.

1717
01:28:55.242 --> 01:28:57.411
Thinking I'm crazy, don't you?
Y'all think I'm crazy,

1718
01:28:57.544 --> 01:28:59.146
but I knew, I told you all.

1719
01:28:59.612 --> 01:29:02.883
You fucking Baker, new kid,
all of you, told you.

1720
01:29:03.017 --> 01:29:05.119
[roaring in the distance]

1721
01:29:06.687 --> 01:29:09.957
-[grunts]
-Listen, focus on your job.
What was that?

1722
01:29:10.091 --> 01:29:12.226
[sighs]
That was just the father Rex.

1723
01:29:12.793 --> 01:29:14.695
Still looking for his family.

1724
01:29:14.829 --> 01:29:16.596
-[roaring continues]
-[sighs]

1725
01:29:16.731 --> 01:29:20.034
-You know that thing can swim.
-[chuckles] It's just animals.

1726
01:29:20.167 --> 01:29:22.470
We stay away from it,
it'll be fine.

1727
01:29:23.270 --> 01:29:25.806
What did you mean before,
that I can't do that?

1728
01:29:25.940 --> 01:29:28.175
[engine rumbling]

1729
01:29:28.309 --> 01:29:31.578
-Collider is unstable.
-[Baker] Right.

1730
01:29:32.213 --> 01:29:34.581
It throws off wormholes
like sparks.

1731
01:29:35.182 --> 01:29:38.085
Space and time are
same thing to wormhole.

1732
01:29:38.853 --> 01:29:41.288
You drop bombs on that,
you will be dropping bombs

1733
01:29:41.422 --> 01:29:43.590
all over the world instantly.

1734
01:29:44.892 --> 01:29:45.993
You ever say something
that doesn't take

1735
01:29:46.127 --> 01:29:47.928
a bad situation
and make it worse?

1736
01:29:48.062 --> 01:29:49.196
[light ominous music]

1737
01:29:49.330 --> 01:29:51.665
I'm Russian and you ask me this.

1738
01:29:51.799 --> 01:29:52.767
[scoffs]

1739
01:29:54.668 --> 01:29:55.669
So, what do we do?

1740
01:29:56.837 --> 01:29:59.373
You must go in and pull plug.

1741
01:30:00.941 --> 01:30:01.809
Do what?

1742
01:30:02.510 --> 01:30:06.247
-Literally, pull plug.
-And what if you're wrong?

1743
01:30:07.547 --> 01:30:09.417
I am never wrong.

1744
01:30:09.549 --> 01:30:12.520
[Miller]
Sarge, situation up here.

1745
01:30:16.023 --> 01:30:17.992
[roaring and grumbling
in the distance]

1746
01:30:18.125 --> 01:30:19.994
-What do you got?
-Over there.

1747
01:30:26.167 --> 01:30:27.735
It's just animals grazing.

1748
01:30:28.335 --> 01:30:30.071
We stay away from them,
we'll be fine.

1749
01:30:31.205 --> 01:30:34.308
[grumbling]

1750
01:30:35.309 --> 01:30:36.210
[Miller]
Think they're harmless?

1751
01:30:36.343 --> 01:30:38.379
[splashing]

1752
01:30:39.080 --> 01:30:40.948
Oh, fuck. Shit!

1753
01:30:44.985 --> 01:30:46.420
[Baker]
We stay the course, Xavier.

1754
01:30:47.455 --> 01:30:49.622
-Hey, hey, put that down!
-No, I need it!

1755
01:30:49.757 --> 01:30:51.591
-Fucking drop it. Fucking drop--
-I need it, give it to me!

1756
01:30:51.725 --> 01:30:53.994
-[Eli] Let go of that, lady!
-I need the morphine.

1757
01:30:54.128 --> 01:30:54.962
[screams]

1758
01:30:55.096 --> 01:30:56.629
[roaring]

1759
01:30:56.764 --> 01:30:58.999
-[splashing]
-[dramatic music]

1760
01:30:59.133 --> 01:31:00.167
Get on that.

1761
01:31:00.868 --> 01:31:03.070
[gunshots]

1762
01:31:05.272 --> 01:31:06.407
The fuck was that?

1763
01:31:07.041 --> 01:31:09.076
[muffled growling]

1764
01:31:13.481 --> 01:31:16.450
-[breathes shakily]
-You need to get
your shit together

1765
01:31:16.584 --> 01:31:18.119
'cause we're doing
what you want.

1766
01:31:18.886 --> 01:31:21.021
And we're probably all gonna die
screaming because of it.

1767
01:31:21.155 --> 01:31:23.324
Can we talk about that
screaming and dying bit?

1768
01:31:23.858 --> 01:31:25.292
Hey, hey, focus.

1769
01:31:26.694 --> 01:31:29.563
-What was that?
-[Sofia breathing shakily]

1770
01:31:29.697 --> 01:31:31.031
Spinosaurus.

1771
01:31:31.699 --> 01:31:33.734
Uh, we have to, to hurry.

1772
01:31:34.435 --> 01:31:35.870
[Miller]
You need me to tie her up?

1773
01:31:40.007 --> 01:31:41.575
Smoke these. Hmm?

1774
01:31:42.409 --> 01:31:45.079
Cope, the American way.

1775
01:31:46.580 --> 01:31:48.015
-[softly] Yeah.
-[Baker] No.

1776
01:31:48.149 --> 01:31:49.717
I think she's gonna be
just fine.

1777
01:31:50.584 --> 01:31:51.452
Right?

1778
01:31:52.720 --> 01:31:53.787
[gunshot]

1779
01:31:54.622 --> 01:31:57.191
-Son of a bitch, stay on that.
-What, they can
fucking swim now?

1780
01:31:57.791 --> 01:31:59.226
Should've seen 'em fucking fly.

1781
01:31:59.360 --> 01:32:00.294
[gunshot]

1782
01:32:02.630 --> 01:32:03.497
[exhales deeply]

1783
01:32:04.298 --> 01:32:06.400
-[suspenseful music]
-[grumbling in the distance]

1784
01:32:07.568 --> 01:32:09.403
[Logan]
Breathe. Relax.

1785
01:32:10.070 --> 01:32:11.772
Aim. Squeeze.

1786
01:32:13.741 --> 01:32:16.610
[roaring and grumbling]

1787
01:32:26.487 --> 01:32:28.756
[Logan softly]
Relax. Aim. Squeeze.

1788
01:32:28.856 --> 01:32:30.591
-[gunshot]
-Logan, shut it down.

1789
01:32:31.358 --> 01:32:32.560
Squeeze.

1790
01:32:33.494 --> 01:32:35.563
I hate 'em. [chuckles]

1791
01:32:35.763 --> 01:32:37.666
[Miller]
Logan, it's okay. Stand down.

1792
01:32:41.869 --> 01:32:42.770
Okay.

1793
01:32:45.105 --> 01:32:46.874
[breathes deeply]

1794
01:32:47.641 --> 01:32:48.642
[Logan]
Okay.

1795
01:32:49.810 --> 01:32:50.844
I'll shut it down.

1796
01:32:51.946 --> 01:32:54.315
I'll sh-- I'll shut it down.

1797
01:32:54.448 --> 01:32:56.483
[light melancholic music]

1798
01:32:57.851 --> 01:32:59.086
I'll shut it down.

1799
01:33:01.589 --> 01:33:02.856
I'll shut it down.

1800
01:33:05.793 --> 01:33:09.330
[exhales softly]
Yeah. You can all go.

1801
01:33:13.133 --> 01:33:14.335
I am gonna go.

1802
01:33:15.369 --> 01:33:17.104
-I--
-[Baker] Hey, hey,
hey, hey. Hey, dude.

1803
01:33:17.238 --> 01:33:19.708
[exhaling sharply]

1804
01:33:21.175 --> 01:33:22.810
You t-- you told me
to shut it down.

1805
01:33:22.876 --> 01:33:24.445
-Yeah, it's not
your time, brother.
-I was just--

1806
01:33:24.578 --> 01:33:26.715
-Hey. It's not your time.
-What?

1807
01:33:26.847 --> 01:33:29.950
-No? Are you sure?
-No. Yeah. I need ya.

1808
01:33:30.884 --> 01:33:32.319
-I feel...
-We need you.

1809
01:33:32.453 --> 01:33:34.021
...I can't feel anything.

1810
01:33:35.823 --> 01:33:37.692
I can't feel anything anymore.

1811
01:33:41.495 --> 01:33:44.031
-Okay. Yeah.
-Huh?

1812
01:33:45.532 --> 01:33:46.400
Yeah.

1813
01:33:47.702 --> 01:33:48.569
I can do this.

1814
01:33:49.470 --> 01:33:50.404
Yeah, I know.

1815
01:33:53.474 --> 01:33:56.443
-I know.
-Yeah. I'm good.

1816
01:34:00.047 --> 01:34:02.549
[breathes loudly]

1817
01:34:06.887 --> 01:34:09.156
[music increases]

1818
01:34:23.470 --> 01:34:26.106
[inhales sharply, groans]

1819
01:34:27.041 --> 01:34:28.409
Make it stop.

1820
01:34:29.877 --> 01:34:30.978
Stay hydrated.

1821
01:34:32.880 --> 01:34:33.981
-[grunts]
-[Baker speaks indistinctly]

1822
01:34:34.114 --> 01:34:35.382
Think the sergeant likes her?

1823
01:34:36.884 --> 01:34:38.886
[Sofia]
The drug
must leave your system--

1824
01:34:38.952 --> 01:34:40.487
The sergeant's
just doing his job.

1825
01:34:41.388 --> 01:34:43.991
...can guarantee you,
dinosaurs have ventured

1826
01:34:44.124 --> 01:34:48.028
into Cambodia. In months,
they could be in Burma,

1827
01:34:48.162 --> 01:34:49.930
in China, in India.

1828
01:34:51.598 --> 01:34:54.034
Once they run out of food
in jungle,

1829
01:34:55.069 --> 01:34:57.604
where do you think
they're going to go to eat?

1830
01:34:59.106 --> 01:35:00.107
We'll stop them.

1831
01:35:01.141 --> 01:35:03.310
-[Sofia] Huh.
-You ready for this?

1832
01:35:05.546 --> 01:35:06.947
[sighs] Face my past?

1833
01:35:08.082 --> 01:35:08.916
Not really.

1834
01:35:09.049 --> 01:35:11.085
[light melancholic music]

1835
01:35:12.553 --> 01:35:15.255
Just smile, pull the trigger,
the problem goes away.

1836
01:35:16.457 --> 01:35:17.925
It's also the American way.

1837
01:35:18.760 --> 01:35:19.626
[whistles]

1838
01:35:21.295 --> 01:35:23.530
["Revolution Road" by Easton]

1839
